{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/11952-1001-werewolf-story-hooks","id":11952,"title":"1001 Werewolf Story Hooks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-16T01:24:21-08:00","id":11952,"title":"1001 Werewolf Story Hooks","content":"Reposting my old 1001 Werewolf Story Hooks thread here, because that sort of thread tends to be useful.<br /> <br /> Please be aware that the numbers won't be consecutive - I created this thread on three separate fora.<br /> <br /> 1) The PC pack has reason to believe that the alpha of a neighboring Forsaken pack has been corrupted by the Maeljin.<br /> <br /> What to do? The PCs lack evidence; and there is no court to appeal. The Forsaken in this particular territory are in no way organized; it's each pack against the world. The only ones who might care might be the Bale Hound's packmates, if they could be made to listen.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 2. Something is mutilating cattle in the PCs' territory. What is it? And how does it turn the poor beasts inside out without cutting them?<br /> <br /> 3. An upstart Storm Lord with delusions of grandeur has called a meet of all the packs in the area. A few more than expected actually show up. He makes a speech, offering to lead them all on a glorious crusade against their enemies, but it's clear he's bitten off more than he can chew. Tempers flare. The crowd starts to turn on him. The fool is about to be ripped apart. What do the PCs do?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 2) This Bale Hound passes himself off as an Uragarum (Wolf-Heart Lies), he's charming and incredibly good looking, and he's blessed by Carnala. He's sired half a dozen of Ghost Childs, his previous mates dead at the hand of the monstrosities, like several other packs. His personal Maeltinent totem is actually an ancestor spirit from his bloodline. It controls the Unihars with it's influence. A Brethren pack has formed to hunt him down. You are in that pack. You never thought you'd hunt besides the Anshega, but the distinctions doesn't matter anymore. The only thing that matters is vengeance now. And you'll have it, or die trying.<br /> <br /> 2) The pack might gain the support of one of the local tribal elders by doing him a little favor.<br /> <br /> One of the elder's wolfblooded daughters has violated family rules by dating a teenager who, sadly, lacks Father Wolf's blood. The PCs are to kill him to send a message and make a point about disobedience.<br /> <br /> The hapless teenager, of course, knows nothing about the Uratha.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 5) One of your few Forsaken allies approaches you after she has been chased out of her territory by her own pack.<br /> <br /> She has nowhere else to go other than to the Pcs. She's pregnant with Ghost Child.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 6) An ancient Lodge of Garm warrior - representing the best of the Blood Talons, a living legend, really - wants to die. The only way for a someone like her to die is in combat, of course - taking as many enemies as possible with her.<br /> <br /> This is why she's planning a proper old-fashioned suicide mission. Break into the territories of Pure packs. Slaughter the Pure and all their allies. Move to the next Pure territory and repeat.<br /> <br /> Volunteers ready to deal with things such as reconaissance, planning etc. are always welcome.<br /> <br /> The fallout of such a mission - no matter the success - will be huge. The Pure and the Forsaken have been living in a state of mutual noninterference for a while. An open attack will likely cause repercussions and retaliation from the Pure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 7) Black Wolf doesn't speak to her children any more. Since last friday, the Hunters in Darkness - all of them - have ceased to feel any sort of connection to their tribal totem. It's as if they were Ghost Wolves, metaphysically. This also means that it's harder for the former Hunters in Darkness to invoke gifts powered by their spiritual patron and to gain the support of her spirit allies.<br /> <br /> It's about time for someone to quest into the Shadow, track down the Black Wolf (good luck with that!) and ask her what the hell is going on.<br /> <br /> If she still exists. And if she's still on the side of the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 7) Spirits around the local university are behaving strangely. There have been more than a few incidences of bizarre and dangerous magath stalking the Shadow of the college. After doing a little digging, the PCs turn up rumors of a secret club of students and faculty performing ancient dionysian rites in the theater building...<br /> <br /> 8) PCs in an urban territory get a call from their police contact. Someone tossed a tourist off the top of a 50-story building after stripping him naked and covering him in blue paint. Police shut off the building and questioned everyone inside, but they've got no suspects. Detective on the case wants to call it a suicide. But maybe the pack wants to look into it...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 9) A werewolf who looks to have had his renown or auspice marks burnt off comes to the pack. He freely admits that he is of the Fire Touched, and the Pure, but says that he wants to join the People once more. He gives a heart rending tale of how he was captured away from his pack, tortured for months, and only allowed his freedom once he agreed to join the Pure and renounce the Moon. He has killed Forsaken, and for many years he truly believed in the cause of the Pure. But now he has found companionship with a wolf-blood, and over several months has had a developing relationship where the two have fallen deeper and deeper in love. The wolf-blood is one of the player's sisters, and rather than be at war with his beloved's family, he comes seeking redemption and repatriation.<br /> The twist here is that everything he says is true, and his intent is honourable. The other twist is that Mother Luna has no intention of taking a Pure back into her People.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 11) The Lodge of Nebuchadnezzar is a group of werewolves lead by a charismatic former rabbi who believes being a werewolf is a curse that can be shed through devotion and service to God. He claims that he has been cured through his good works and encourages Uratha to deny their wolf side. The Lodge is in violation of the Oath of the Moon, but its members are otherwise blameless and innocent. A local pack has targeted the lodge for destruction. Meanwhile, the members of the Lodge of Nebuchadnezzar are out of harmony with their true nature, and it's only a matter of time before the beast within claws its way to the surface...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 12) A massive hurricane has been battering Florida and parts of the East Coast of the USA for several weeks now, to the confusion and bafflement of mundane meteorologists. Forsaken looking into the matter have found out that this is no ordinary storm: this is the rage of Winter Wolf, who is angry at something or someone in the area. A pack of high ranking Storm Lords (aka, the player characters) have taken it on themselves to remedy the situation, as the storm is growing, the East Coast is getting ravaged, and people are dying. They can recruit whatever help they want, and approach this however they want, though if they're smart, they'll remember their tribal Oath when sorting out their tribe's own mess.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 13) That girl you slept with after the party? The granddaughter of the nastiest Bone Shadow wolf witch in the entire state. She generally takes &quot;The People Do Not Murder The People&quot; seriously, but that just means she'll make you wish you were dead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 14) They've been talking about turning that one shitty neighborhood around for a while now. However, right before that nice urban renewal project is to get started, the funding gets pulled, a couple community organizers wind up dead, and to add insult to injury, somebody's trashed the construction site of that shiny new community center.<br /> <br /> The culprits, as it turns out, are a group of Hunters in Darkness who've found a balance with the various spirits of poverty, addiction, violence, and urban blight that infest the area, and see anybody trying to change the spiritual ecosystem as a threat to said balance.<br /> <br /> Sure it'd be nice to clean up the area, and those guys are probably nuts, but what if their dire predictions of events if the city's Shadow is changed are correct?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 8) During the Bretheren War, the Urdaga of the region managed to unite against the Pure and hold on to their territory thanks to the leadership of a Storm Lord alpha. Since then, he's been turned to for keeping the peace between the packs. But over the years, he has taken the trust that was put in him and used it to gain more and more power. A few years ago he gave himself the title &quot;Chieftain.&quot;<br /> <br /> The PCs are newly-changed and waiting for this Chieftain to decide which packs should have whom. In the first act of defiance against the Chieftain in years, they choose to become their own pack and claim a territory on the outskirts of Urdaga control. They've inspired some of the other packs to rise up and overthrow the Chieftain. War's coming, and one way or another, the PCs will have to pick a side.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 9) Your pack's totem did something to piss off pretty much every choir and spirit court in the local Shadow.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 10) The PCs are chasing after a dangerous spirit that manifested across the Gauntlet in their territory, and possessed a close friend or family member of one of the PC's. However, they realize soon that they are trespassing deep into Pure territory. Was this a trap? How did the spirit slip through the Gauntlet in their territory, unimpeded without their totem or allied spirits noticing? Will the PCs continue pursuing after the friend/family member, or are they wary of springing a Pure ambush that may initiate a war?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 17) The Lodge of Mammon is using Vampire mercenaries to abduct Wolf-Bloodeds that they sell to a Baal-Hadad cult.<br /> <br /> 18) One of the local Forsaken has been feeding on human prey. The PCs need to find out who it is, because the seriously armed government-backed hunter cell who just arrived in town thinks it's them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 19) A Pure werewolf breaches the pack's territory and upon capture claims to be defecting, having received visions from Death Wolf herself. She seems to be telling the truth. The pack and neighbouring Pure have been in a detente situation for years, with the Pure outnumbering the Forsaken three to one. Will they risk war over her?<br /> <br /> 20) A long-time ally of the pack is revealed to be a Bale Hound infiltrator. Before the pack can expose him for what he is, he turns the other Forsaken against the pack, accusing them of being what he is. Now the pack has to protect itself from enraged friends and family, while trying to stop their one-time ally from carrying out his nefarious plan.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 21) An old-name Keralan family with a distant but existent blood relation to one of the player characters is wolf-blooded, and aware of it. They are keen to maximise the chance of having a werewolf child in the next generation and have proud and ancient links to the People, with many of the Uratha's greatest heroes in the last six centuries being born from their bloodline.<br /> For that reason are looking for male Uratha applicants to be married to a young wolf-blood girl of the family, who has just turned 16. They're keen for her to have kids, and have the support network in place that the Uratha will know that his children will be raised in a supportive environment, educated in the ways of the People and will be well protected.<br /> They've singled out one of the players as a potential match, and have sent an elderly aunt to size him up and make the offer.<br /> The twist is this: there is no coercion, nothing weird going on here. This is just an ancient bloodline looking to keep the wolf blood strong, with a young girl who is entirely willing to be married to someone of her parent's choosing, and who honestly believes that love comes after marriage, not before it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 22) The PCs are chasing after a dangerous spirit that manifested across the Gauntlet in their territory, and possessed a close friend or family member of one of the PC's. However, they soon realize that they are trespassing deep into Pure territory. Was this a trap? How did the spirit slip through the Gauntlet in their territory, unimpeded without their totem or allied spirits noticing? Will the PCs continue pursuing after the friend/family member, or are they wary of springing a Pure ambush that may initiate a war?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 23) One fairly inexperienced pack seems to have a lot more Essence than you'd expect, given the size of their territory,. A brief investigation reveals the reason: they've formed an alliance with a Beshilu swarm. The Beshilu gnaw holes in the Gauntlet creating new Loci, while the pack protect them and keep their activities concealed. This utter abandonment of their duties would (under ordinary circumstances) get them driven out or even killed, but there's a major conflict with the Pure looming, and losing the abundant new Essence sources and the huge numbers of spirit allies they're bribing with it would put the Forsaken at a serious disadvantage. What to do?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 24) A group of weirdos have arrived in and whatever they're doing has started stirring up spirits of despair and death all over the place. It's getting so bad that locals have started forming death cults worshipping some strange &quot;Judges of the Dead.&quot; One of the local packs went to &quot;talk&quot; to them about it, but left the meeting battered and bruised. The survivors say that whoever these the things leading these people are are, they're not human. They're too strong, too durable, and when they use their strange power they look like the living dead. What will the pack do about these strange interlopers? What do they want with/in the surrounding area? Can be negotiated with? And if not, can they be made to leave? Something needs to happen fast, because their power is throwing the local spirit courts dangerously out of whack.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 25) A local politician who signed a wolf-hunting law suddenly repeals it, and in a startling turnabout actually starts to lobby for preservation and expansion of wild areas. The local wolves, unfortunately, have been hunted to extinction \u2014 but a vengeful wolf-spirit is slowly taking control of the politician and driving him to ever more lupine behavior. Worse still, the wolf-spirit is on the verge of becoming magath before it ever Claims its host, because it has fed on the pain, fear and anger of the wolf hunts. It also has no concept of discretion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 26) The Cahalith of the pack has had dreams about some young guy undergoing his First Change as a Full Moon. The pack has tracked him down successfully - he's currently in prison.<br /> <br /> If the Cahalith's prophecy is accurate, he's likely to become a werewolf within the week.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 27) The Cahalith of the pack has regular nightmares of one of the pack's Forsaken allies - one of their mentors, perhaps - turning Bale Hound.<br /> <br /> There is no evidence of these nightmares being in any way true. The ally is known to value the Oath of the Moon particularly highly, and has always been friendly to the PCs.<br /> <br /> <br /> 28) While the PCs were busy with another problem within their territory, an Azlu incursion got way out of hand. The PCs' own locus and several other loci are now completely cut off. Only one locus is still open, and it leads into the heart of the web, and a waiting ambush that is sure to decimate the pack. The PCs might sneak into the gauntlet through a locus a hundred miles away and a couple territories over...but that locus belongs to one of the Pure tribes...<br /> <br /> 29) The PCs have broken the law and tangled with the human authorities a couple times within their territory. One cop in particular has been a thorn in their side. That cop has just been Claimed by a Justice spirit. And it's no coincidence. Some enemy shaman among the Uratha played &quot;matchmaker&quot; between the spirit and the cop...<br /> <br /> .) A spirit of justice starts to possess people, forcing them to fight crime. That's a good thing. Right?<br /> <br /> .) The PCs, all of which are rather new to this werewolf thing, find themselves being hungrier than usual. They also start fantasizing about consuming human flesh.<br /> <br /> Clearly, someone or something is influencing them in some way. These urges are in no way a natural part of the werewolf condition. Right?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 32) A pack allied with the PCs makes heavy use of Spirit-Ridden allies on its hunts. The pack gives spirits permission to Claim people, providing that the Claimed then assist the pack when dealing with the Hosts or the Pure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 33) Something terrible happened, and your brother's house is on fire.<br /> <br /> Trouble is, he resides in a block of the city that belongs to a particularly territory-conscious Hunter in Darkness pack. There's no way they'll let you in, not even in the case of an absolute emergency.<br /> <br /> They might not notice you sneaking in, but there will absolutely be retribution for trespassing.<br /> <br /> <br /> 34) The neighbouring pack, who you've never liked much, were recently involved in a mundane but fatal (to all but one pack member) car accident in the motorway. Four werewolves are dead, mauled by a high speed pile up that left their jalopy crushed under the weight of an eighteen wheeler. One Uratha, the runt of the group, survived and did so only because he was extremely lucky. He's still in hospital right now, sowly healing injuries that would have left a human a paraplegic (severed spinal cord, multiple organs punctured and failing). The players are called in by him because he needs them to help cover his tracks, as he isn't in any position to hide his presence at the moment (he can't get out of the hospital bed yet) and the medical establishment are getting a bit too interested in his miraculous rate of recovery. Of course, once they've done this relatively simple job for him, he tells them about all the other troubles his pack's territory has, and asks if he can join their pack, and if they can take over the territory.<br /> Can the players deal with a new territory that is larger and more troublesome than the one they already had? If they don't, are they willing to let the Pure on the far side of that territory move in? And do they want an extra packmate, when they never liked him that much in the first place?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 35) When an entire pack dies in a territorial dispute, their totem spirit is cut loose. Confused, angry and overcome with grief, it begins to agitate the local spirit populace against all of the Forsaken. It needs to be put down.<br /> <br /> 36) The PCs tangle with a pack of Predator Kings who show up in their territory one day out of the blue. These Pure usually stick to the desolate wilderness outside of town. The Predator Kings aren't invading. They're running. Something from within their territory is hunting them.<br /> <br /> 37) You told your niece to stay away from that night club. You didn't tell her the reason: that vampires are known to congregate there. Now you're getting a call from her mother. She never came home last night. [I'd probably let the PCs start a full-scale vamp/wolf war before they realize that she hooked up with a normal human guy and didn't even have sex with him. Just passed out on his couch]<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 38) On October 11, 11:33 am CET, all werewolves on the planet - Forsaken, Pure, Bale Hound, etc. - feel that the world has changed irrevocably. As they hear a howl of unimaginable savagery, they all know - it's Father Wolf. He's back.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 38) A ghost wolf of considerable mental fortitude and academic nous (Willpower 10, 5 dots in Occult with a specialty in werewolves) approaches the pack - by distant communication first - to tell them that he has identified them as Uratha, but that his discretion is guaranteed. He wishes to inform them of some interesting statistics. If they agree to meet or correspond with them he presents to them info showing that for the world and the world population distribution, there aren't nearly enough werewolves to police the gauntlet, and that the vast majority of the world has no Forsaken looking over it, nor any Pure or other wolves. He also has data about spirit incursions, and he has come to an astounding conclusion. Werewolves are the problem, not the cure.<br /> As far as he can tell, where loci go unused, rates of problems with spirits affecting the human world drop rapidly. In fact, in areas with no werewolves at all, there is almost no problem with the spirit world and world of matter staying apart and in harmony. It seems to be the presence of werewolves that correlates with disruptions, and that the more werewolves use loci, and the more powerful they are, the more problems occur.<br /> His findings call into challenge the very role of werewolves. They aren't protecting the people, they're like plague dogs, bringing problems with their very presence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 39) After several very tense months when the Pure were showing sign of preparing for a massive invasion, they've gone quiet. Their probes into Forsaken territory have stopped altogether. Since something is clearly wrong, so your pack decides to make a quick little recon into Pure territory. There, you find a greatly weakened spirit known to be one of the enemy's totems. With the information you get from it, you figure out what happened.<br /> <br /> An Idigam has appeared, and it's starting with the Pure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 40) 18 years ago on this date, a horrible mass murder occurred in the PCs territory. They just took over the territory within the last few months, so they don't know that on the anniversary, the spirit of that day gains immense power and stirs up an unholy nest of grief, sorrow, fear and trauma spirits. The PCs enter the Hisil on a routine errand, not realizing that when the clock hits midnight, they're going to be walking right into the middle of a war zone.<br /> <br /> 41) A particularly ancient Forsaken, immensely potent and the subject of no few local legends, has awoken from several centuries of deep slumber in the hisil. There's an lodge dedicated to her memory, and packs from all over are anxious to recruit her as an ally or patron. Unfortunately, she's completely out of her depth in the current century. Her attitudes towards the Pure are completely at odds with the current status quo, she thinks practically all technology spirits are at best magath and at worst the corrupt spawn of some idigam, she's trying to reclaim the territory that originally belonged to her (at least some of which belongs to the pack) and she has so far refused to change her mind or understand how different things are now. The Forsaken community risks splintering into various factions who wish variously to use her, worship her, learn from her or kill her. How is the pack going to deal with this?<br /> <br /> 42) A powerful Forsaken, an ally of the pack and a mentor of one of the PCs, someone they consider to be a close friend and something of a spiritual guide, has very recently done what nobody ever expected him to do - he defected to the Predator Kings.<br /> <br /> The PCs know him as an exceedingly wise old wolf; he wouldn't become a Predator King without an excellent reason.<br /> <br /> 20) One of the PCs is the youngest heir to an ancient, rich bloodline of royalty among wolves - all of his werewolf relatives are Predator Kings. And they desperately want the PC to join the family, by any means necessary.<br /> <br /> <br /> 43) There's a stranger in town, and when he comes near, Uratha can't control their shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> 44) A new type of cellular network has been introduced to the area. Suddenly, ALL the technology spirits in the territory start to aggregate and merge with one another. By the time the PCs arrive in the Hisil, the gestalt tech spirit is an enormous godzilla-size demigod of wires and lightning, playing with the city like a toy...<br /> <br /> <br /> 45) One of the tribal elders is displaying a frighteningly low level of Harmony. It's time for an intervention.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 46) The paranormal teen romance novel Dusk Part 2: Stalker's Moon has werewolf characters modeled so closely on the Uratha that it can't be a coincidence. The herd must not know. The author...or whoever gave her the information...must die.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 47) A packmate reveals that she's pregnant. She also reveals that the father is a werewolf from a neighboring pack.<br /> <br /> Related...<br /> <br /> 48) A friendly pack reveals that one of their number has given birth to a child fathered by a packmate ... and the child is Uratha.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 49) There's a whole load of excavation and quarrying work going on as new fracking site is being prepped. The funny thing is that they found a whole load of tunnels and caves which didn't show on the surveys and security there is super-tight and super antsy. The really funny thing is that they say that they're finding a whole load of stuff in there, including loads of very old documents and books.<br /> <br /> The unfunny thing is that you're hearing that the books are weird and you were told details, and I quote 'a way of stuffing rats into a person so that they can control the person and they can turn into a swarm of rats and stuff like that'.<br /> <br /> The really unfunny thing is that apparently the books are going missing.<br /> <br /> 50) The PC pack is being framed for oath violations that they didn't commit. Very soon, the tribal elders will want their heads.<br /> <br /> 51) Faced with a problem they can't deal with the pack set out to get advice from their tribal elders. Conventional means of long distance communication aren't working though - telephone calls aren't being picked up, post is being returned, emails are bouncing, and it looks as if the Iron Master elder who keeps a facebook account hasn't logged in for some moons. Worse still, it looks as if every werewolf they contact seems to have become incommunicado. Spirit messages aren't getting through either - messengers report they can't find their targets.<br /> It suddenly looks as if the werewolves are alone in the world, and that the entire People (themselves excluded) has disappeared. They haven't tried contacting the nearest Pure yet. What now?<br /> <br /> 53) A local pack reveals to the PCs that many years ago they made a deal with something powerful that was not a spirit. Since then, each year for a whole night they are under the thrall of this creature, a elfin man who shines like the moon and has hair like thistle-down, to hunt down mortals who stray into the woods at night...<br /> <br /> 54) A mortal who the werewolves had to kill is apparently still alive and kicking, though he seems to talk to himself much more now...<br /> <br /> 55) A group of magi have made their way into town and are now monkeying around with the spirit world, warping it into something more 'harmonious to the Primal Wilds', whatever the fuck that means.<br /> <br /> 56) Clockwork wolves have been stalking the hills at night.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T10:00:19-08:00","id":14141,"title":"","content":"57) Members of the pack find themselves being followed ... by cats. Ordinary housecats keep following them everywhere they go.<br /> <br /> There doesn't appear to be anything unnatural about the cats - they aren't possessed by spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T15:55:43-08:00","id":14343,"title":"","content":"58) Lunacy stops working.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T07:12:41-08:00","id":19157,"title":"","content":"59) A powerful spirit of lethargy gains control of the PC's territory in the Shadow. The other spirits would gladly break the spirit's dominance, but eh, why bother?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T06:21:52-08:00","id":19690,"title":"","content":"60) A vampire nearby has uncovered the benefits from drinking werewolf blood and has begun kidnapping werewolves on a large scale to &quot;commercialize&quot; his product for all vampires. However this vampire so far has only been taking pack members from the pure. Do the players intervene and stop him, aiding their enemies? Or do they wait until he starts taking forsaken as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1387-moxy","name":"Moxy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1387_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T13:01:05-08:00","id":19870,"title":"","content":"61) Everything has been quiet on the Beshilu front for years, but rats all around the territory (just plain ordinary rats) are starting to act in wildly erratic and aggressive ways.<br /> <br /> The Cahalith PC has disturbing dreams about a Plague King rebuilding his body from thousands of rats and eating the wall between the Shadow and the Flesh. Not just parts of it - all of it. Everywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T13:04:33-08:00","id":19872,"title":"","content":"62) The PCs know for sure that of the three people in the room other than the pack, one of them has a spider in her brain. They need to find a way to tell which one, and quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T13:07:23-08:00","id":19874,"title":"","content":"63) An Azlu, of all things, contacts the pack with an offer - it'll tell them the location of an assortment of powerful fetishes that have once been given to the Forsaken by the Firstborn totems themselves. All it want in exchange is a new, human host body.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T16:06:02-08:00","id":24719,"title":"","content":"64/ Ithaeurs do not received essence when they saw crescent moon in the sky. The local ithalunim has been missing or worst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1549-obiwankennedy","name":"ObiWanKennedy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T19:00:20-08:00","id":24837,"title":"","content":"65) There was a massive earthquake during an eclipse. The Hisil is in an uproar as the world changes and emotions pour fourth in chaotic waves. The lunes don't know what happened, and other spirits of knowledge and secrets are also at a loss. People are claiming its the end of the world, and while it's easy to scoff, Something has changed. You can feel it in the resonances, tainted by something you can't quite name. The Gauntlet is thinner, people are being affected by the chaos, doing things they normally wouldn't. Time to get to the bottom of it.<br /> 65b) For added tension, have the werewolves be there as it happens. Perhaps they saw what caused it, or not, but now they have to navigate their way through a disastrous spirit landscape or unstable cityscape to get the word out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T08:26:05-08:00","id":30981,"title":"","content":"66/A group of inexperienced mages uses silver bullets on Pure. All urathas of the city want them to stop. Forsakens think it is a sin. Pure werewolves want them dead.<br /> How far the forsakens are ready to go to protect their brothers to be victim of such a sin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1549,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1549-obiwankennedy","user":"ObiWanKennedy","date":". 03-03-2014, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1549-obiwankennedy","name":"ObiWanKennedy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T07:31:10-08:00","id":33172,"title":"","content":"67) A large loci has been set up underneath a very thick azlu barrier, the beshilu of the area have cut trenches leading from this barrier across the city A large spirit coming through the portal could literally SNAP the gauntlet into shreds removing it forever. Worse still, who got the azlu and the beshilu working together?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1387-moxy","name":"Moxy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1387_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T02:01:24-08:00","id":78185,"title":"","content":"68) It appears as if the longstanding rivalry of two Pure packs hunting near the PC's territory is at an end. The PCs get word that the two packs are to meet to discuss a probable alliance ni the near future.<br /> <br /> This must not be allowed to happen - the PCs need to find a way to make sure the Pure continue their rivalry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T16:38:57-08:00","id":80609,"title":"","content":"69) You're at the hospital visiting a relative who just had an incident (car, respiratory...). On one occasion of heading down to the cafeteria you take the stairs (cause screw elevators am I right? Moving death boxes!) and notice that something feels... off about that last door another story down. Opening the door reveals the Hisil...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T16:43:26-08:00","id":80611,"title":"","content":"70) The local ski lodge has been having a sudden influx of homeless breaking into trash cans and eating the contents. That isn't the odd part. The odd part is the alarming increase in home break ins, coupled with the theft of just food. The issue seems to be getting consistently worse each time the pack heads into town or turns on the news. <br /> <br /> Most disturbing of all are the strange reports of the homeless roaming in the forest near bear occupied sites. One hunter even reported an individual attempting to grab a fish from the local river with just his bare hands and teeth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T09:13:51-08:00","id":81621,"title":"","content":"71) A particularly nasty spirit servant of the Maeljin decides to possess a local teacher, and starts to teach hate and extremism and life-denying belief to little kids.<br /> <br /> The teacher is particularly well-entrenched and loved by society, and it'll be very difficult to hunt and/or get close to her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T10:30:36-08:00","id":81653,"title":"","content":"72) The pack has the honor of being invited to the wedding of two local spirits.<br /> <br /> Never mind the fact that the concept of a wedding should be, metaphysically, incompatible with spirits. They're still getting married. And they want the player characters to show up as guests of honor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T10:33:05-08:00","id":81655,"title":"","content":"73) The spirits are strangely quiet. The Pure haven't been seen in months. The PCs have very recently destroyed the last local Azlu nest, and if there are any rats in town, they're keeping quiet as well. Things are going well on the mortal side, tool.<br /> <br /> It's like the territory, collectively, decided to take things easy and let the pack relax.<br /> <br /> Something is very wrong here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T10:37:54-08:00","id":81659,"title":"","content":"74) A Blood Talon from a neighboring pack has taken a liking to your wolf-blooded sister.<br /> <br /> The Blood Talon isn't exactly known for his self-control. Ex-girlfriends have been hit and/or cut and put in hospital and a grave yard (almost), before.<br /> <br /> Very soon you notice her desperately trying to hide bruises from you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T10:39:03-08:00","id":81660,"title":"","content":"75) A Predator King from a neighboring pack has taken a liking to your wolf-blooded sister.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T10:48:43-08:00","id":81665,"title":"","content":"76) Janos Kardassian is a nice, unassuming man. Unemployed, since recently been laid off. Divorced. Two kids. Werewolf senses would likely notice that he has a little drinking problem; other than that, there is nothing extraordinary about him. In the Flesh, at least.<br /> <br /> In the Shadow, Janos Kardassian is constantly followed around by a rather huge host of shadowy entities. They read his thoughts. They follow his subconscious's wishes. One of the spirits has recently burned down his former boss's apartment. The spirits are ready and prepared to do anything and everything Janos wants.<br /> <br /> There is no reason and no explanation. There is no trace of wolf blood in Jano's veins, and he has never knowingly experienced anything remotely supernatural himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T10:51:01-08:00","id":81667,"title":"","content":"77) There is a new pack in town. They say they're fighting for the Idigam. There is no other option, in their opinion. Resistance against the Idigam is futile, basically.<br /> <br /> They say they give you 24 hours to decide whether to join them or be hunted down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T10:57:40-08:00","id":82167,"title":"","content":"78) (For a Pure chronicle) The city has been a stronghold for the <i>Anshega </i>for the last twelve years, after the three tribes united under the (temporary) leadership of a clever Fire-Touched alpha and very nearly exterminated the <i>Urdaga</i>. But recently, relations between the tribes have become strained, and every indication is that things will only get worse. On the increasingly-rare occasion that the packs have a meeting, old grudges keep coming up without resolution and new grudges appear almost every other week.<br /> <br /> Your pack is the only one with members from each of the three tribes. You've staked out a territory on the outskirts, where you can watch for activity from Luna's minions. You do this because no one else will. One day, your totem informs you that a Silver Crusade is coming--the Forsaken are preparing to invade and re-conquer the city, and they have the numbers, the weapons and the allies to do this. The Pure have little hope of victory. Your totem goes on to say that you should be looking out for each other now, putting your pack first, and that survival may require you to consider...new ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","user":"Daydreamer","date":". 03-02-2014, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T00:15:30-08:00","id":87307,"title":"","content":"79) Practically overnight, a potent locus has formed within your pack's territory. You desperately need the essence it can provide, but a human wizard's magic somehow keeps werewolves and spirits alike from drawing on it without permission. If things get physical, the pack quickly learns that the warrior-wizard who created the locus is more than capable of throwing down with an angry werewolf or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T11:42:27-07:00","id":88325,"title":"","content":"71) The Refugium is a place that isn't - that is, a location in the Shadow that doesn't have an equivalent in the Flesh. Only very few werewolves know about its existence and how to reach it, and it should take long and hard quests through the deepest reaches of the spirit wilds to find it on one's own.<br /> <br /> To werewolf senses, the Refugium appears to be Pangaea resurrected. There is plenty of prey to be hunted, and the Uratha have the opportunity to rule as kings over lesser creatures and animals. The entire place is flowing with Essence, and werewolves should get all kinds of system advantages while in the Refugium, like faster regeneration, more powerful forms and extra gift dice. Werewolves should feel welcome.<br /> <br /> So welcome, in fact, that they might never want to leave. The Refugium is, to all intents and purposes, what's left of Pangaea - a lost paradise for the People, a heaven for predators.<br /> <br /> Only the most powerful rites will reveal that this place is actually weakly tainted by the essence of Beliar, Maeljin of Sloth.<br /> <br /> The PCs should feel tempted to stay in Refugium forever. This place offers respite to the horrors of the World of Darkness. There are no Pure, no Hosts, no creatures that hate them because of what they are. There's no suffering, and it feels good to be in a place that accepts the Uratha.<br /> <br /> In the end, the PCs are going to have to decide between their duties as Forsaken werewolves of the Tribes of the Moon, keeping their people and territories safe, or respite from being Forsaken in this heaven specifically designed for them.<br /> <br /> Once you leave the Refugium, there is no turning back. You've forsaken paradise in favor of the World of Darkness, and your decision must be final.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T04:47:57-07:00","id":91545,"title":"","content":"72) A bunch of horrific murders have been taken place that leave locals talking of &quot;werewolf&quot; scares. The victims are shredded while being partially eaten. Instead of being werewolves, they are a human family with corrupted Wolf spirits inside them. They're Skindancers of the old style and while they are no match for a Forsaken pack, they know about werewolves themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T23:31:58-07:00","id":98150,"title":"","content":"73) A little girl goes missing. Only a few days later, the PCs see a cat with the face of the girl in the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Is she a spirit? A new Host? Something stranger?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T07:50:37-07:00","id":101259,"title":"","content":"74) Texas, 1875. A powerful spirit of wrathful justice has gone missing from the Shadow. Now the pack hears stories of a mysterious figure who hunts down and kills fugitives and evil-doers. The killer is said to have a .45 Colt that never runs out of bullets, never misses, and always kills its target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T13:09:52-07:00","id":103609,"title":"","content":"75) The Pure have been more annoying and murderous than usual in the last couple weeks; and many local Forsaken packs have escaped to safer territories and/or defected to the Fire Touched.<br /> <br /> Things get weirder when the PC pack is approached by the cult of a powerful Incarna of peace - the cult and its god needs the PCs to help freeing the Incarna of peace, who is currently stuck inside a fetish. In exchange, the Incarna promises to create lasting peace between the local Pure and Forsaken.<br /> <br /> A local Bone Shadow elder opposes freeing the Incarna adamantly - according to her, the Incarna has been imprisoned inside the fetish for a good reason.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T13:10:46-07:00","id":103610,"title":"","content":"76) A jaggling of desire has possessed a valuable diamond. The spirit uses its power to affect people, making them feel a strong need to own the diamond. People have already gotten hurt as a consequence of the spirit's influence - and not even the Forsaken are immune.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T13:12:59-07:00","id":103611,"title":"","content":"77) The appropriate sacrifices have been performed, the prerequisite chiminage has been offered - all successfully. The prayers of the Fire Touched have been answered - the son of the Wolf God now walks the earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T13:13:41-07:00","id":103612,"title":"","content":"78) The Wolf-Killer, a magath that, as the local Cahalith have been given to understand in their dreams, has been created (by whom?) for the purpose of hunting and killing werewolves, has succeed admirably in its task. Pretty much all local packs have had to bury members, and the Wolf-Killer has still defied attempts to track it down and tear it apart.<br /> <br /> Word has it that the Uratha lack the ability to hunt and destroy the Wolf-Killer. Perhaps someone who doesn't have wolf-blood - a human mortal? - could find its weakness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T10:14:50-07:00","id":104121,"title":"","content":"79) You Wolf-blooded nephew witnessed a First Change and the havoc it caused. Since then he has built a group of hunters, primarily wolf-blooded, for the sake taking down the monsters he know hunts among mankind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T10:16:17-07:00","id":104122,"title":"","content":"80) One day the totem left your pack and went into the spirit wilds, and since then every spririt has been increasingly hostile to the pack to the verge that an all-out war with the Hisil might be coming near.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T10:17:41-07:00","id":104123,"title":"","content":"81) The joy of your daughter having her First Changed turned to horror when the Fire-Touched where there to take her with them. Now you save her before she is lost to the Pure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":970,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","user":"Gurkhal","date":". 04-02-2014, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T10:27:59-07:00","id":104132,"title":"","content":"82) He came lone and half-starved and dirty to your territory and announced his presence. The young Fire-Touched whelp claimed to have escape the Pure and asked for sanctity with the pack. He claims to have information he would trade in return for safe passage and protection but how far does the pack dare to trust him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T12:17:33-07:00","id":104241,"title":"","content":"83) In a dream, the pack's Cahalith sees how most of the local werewolves, barring very few exceptions, secretly worship the Maeljin and offer them sacrifices.<br /> <br /> It can't be one of the prophetic dreams the Cahalith are know for, because the implications would be staggering. Right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T12:21:10-07:00","id":104243,"title":"","content":"84) A rival Forsaken pack deals with undesirable spirits, Ridden and Hosts by chasing them out of its own territory ... and right into yours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T12:28:43-07:00","id":104251,"title":"","content":"85) The spiders are acting up again. But then, so are the Ivory Claws; and it's not like the pack doesn't already have problems in the form of some rather persistent hunger-spirits and their tendency to possess nice, innocent people and give them a taste for human flesh.<br /> <br /> That's when a rather sizey group of human hunters decides to join in the fun and starts to stalk the pack.<br /> <br /> It's time for some desperate measures - such an attempt to get the many enemies of the pack to neutralize each other. Because there's no way the pack will survive otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T08:31:47-07:00","id":104842,"title":"","content":"86) Winter Wolf, the tribal totem of all Storm Lords, approaches the PCs. He is considering defecting to the Pure. He gives the PCs a chance to convince him otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T08:33:18-07:00","id":104844,"title":"","content":"87) A spirit of change and chaos that has gotten on the bad side of the pack Rides people, using its powers of shapechanging to masquerade as the PCs and wreak havoc that the PCs are being blamed for.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T09:11:14-07:00","id":104864,"title":"","content":"88) As you're out, patrolling the Shadow of your territory, you catch the scent of one of the People. Once you get to corner the intruder, it turns out she's a member of a rival pack of Forsaken. She claims to be the only survivor of an attack by a Ralunim. Can she be trusted? Did one of the less than reliable Lune allies finally betray the Forsaken? Did the pack give him reason to do so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T16:10:09-07:00","id":105892,"title":"","content":"89) The dating was good and the nights were great. Only to late did you, and them, realize that the guy you were dating was infact a wolf-blooded to the Ivory Claws and now they are coming down on both of you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T05:19:33-07:00","id":106225,"title":"","content":"90) The plague started with the Forsaken and their wolf-blooded and the Fire-Touched howled in challenge to the Moon for the punishment brought down by Rabid Wolf. Then the Pure caught it and they turned to purification rites and flagellations, and then they started to die as well. All over the city werewolves and wolf-blooded are catching the illness but everyone else is spared.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T11:31:16-07:00","id":106407,"title":"","content":"91) The lineage's ancestor spirit is going berserk over the lack of commitment to traditional values in the present day. The werewolves from this lineage better do something real fast before a whole bunch of wolf-blooded are lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T11:38:40-07:00","id":106411,"title":"","content":"92) &quot;Hi! You know uncle Thomas? He runs with the Iron Nails pack and all that. He learned about Jessica going out with this non-wolf blooded guy and...didn't take it very well. Could you get your ass over there to Jessica? Yeah, right now. Don't stop for anything. Just fucking go!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T11:44:51-07:00","id":106418,"title":"","content":"93) You first thought it was some Ghost Wolf or maybe some brazen young Pure wanting to give you the finger. But it turns it you were wrong. It likes to kill, and is pretty good at it, it hunts like a predator and seems to have claimed territory right here. But it sure as hell isn't Uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T11:51:55-07:00","id":106423,"title":"","content":"94) They whine, bitch and moan 24/7 to you. &quot;Why don't you have any kids?&quot; How long can you stand it, and how do you find a girl who you like and is willing to drag her into the world of the Uratha? Cause all the wolf-blooded chicks are busy elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T09:20:35-07:00","id":106935,"title":"","content":"95) A pack of Hunters in Darkness are growing more and more radical to the point of sharing some viewpoints with the Predator Kings. Someone will need to talk with them and everyone know your pack and theirs goes way pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T11:19:00-07:00","id":110184,"title":"","content":"96. A local cell of &quot;hunters&quot; have been making your life hell. They're not wolf-blooded, but they have some way to resist Lunacy. Are they a threat, or are they a tool against the area Pure? And how did they learn to resist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T13:11:45-07:00","id":121157,"title":"","content":"97) The Firetouched really like you. Their elders have had a vision - straight from the Rabid Wolf themselves, they claim. You are to be their messiah, come to lead them to final victory against the Forsaken. Congratulations!<br /> <br /> This doesn't change the fact that you're still Forsaken, and not planning to defect any time soon. &quot;Yet&quot;, they say. They have ways to change your mind, they say. After all, you are the Chosen One.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T12:41:51-07:00","id":123945,"title":"","content":"98) The Forsaken's connection to the Moon - their auspices - changes all of a sudden. Auspice abilities become significantly more powerful, and auspice gifts cheaper to buy.<br /> <br /> At the same time, werewolves are more bound by the dictates of the auspice than they were before. Rahu feel compelled to seek out battle, Ithaeur can't help being drawn to the Shadow, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T14:39:35-07:00","id":124004,"title":"","content":"99) A number of hunter cells banded together and, in a daring (not to mention astonishingly successful) raid, destroyed the entire ruling court of the city's vampires. Naturally, the leeches have descended into a mad, backstabbing power grab. One of the major figures in this struggle approaches your pack and makes an offer: help him eliminate his rivals, and he will use his influence over mortal affairs to gift you ownership of an office building, all to yourselves--an office building that also happens to house a powerful locus. He'll even help secure the area around it, once you've added it to your territory.<br /> <br /> It sounds too good to pass up--almost to good to be true. Wait, just how does this leech know so much about werewolves and what they would want? If you pass up the offer, he'll take it to another pack, maybe one of your enemies...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T11:39:03-07:00","id":124638,"title":"","content":"100) Some powerful but asshole Ghost Wolf is walking around and destroying fetishes left and right. Just sneaking into territories and smashing, burning and trashing them. You've lost several and enough i enough. You don' know why, but do you really care?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T20:08:35-07:00","id":126395,"title":"","content":"101: There's a new power player in the area your pack patrols. Spirits of technology spiked in number for a few days, but now deadlier magaths of technology and other spirits keep appearing. These are too many to pin down on natural spirit life cycles. It's like someone is purposefully creating magath out of high technology and other spirits.<br /> <br /> 102: The water isn't a natural place for the People to patrol, but stories from the grapevine are picking up. A story about local &quot;hunters&quot; facing down fishmen could've been brushed off as the kill-happy idiots shooting at something they didn't understand, but then you heard about a group of witches that vanished from the beach after researching &quot;something strange&quot;. Hunters you can write off easy. Actual witches? That's a different story. Somethings coming out of the seas.<br /> <br /> 103: Most teenagers, on seeing war-forms, flee in terror and start babbling about sasquatch. Only now a younger pack is running to yours, screaming about a bunch of warriors as young as them using magic to force them away from their territory. They say their attackers have taken up the territory, and that there's been a strange upswing; spirits of hope and love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T12:36:21-07:00","id":129184,"title":"","content":"104) The Beshilu are like gone from the face of the earth. Not a single sound from the rats. Then one day its big news as a whole load of dieses sweeps across your town. Looks like the Plague-King is back i business and he's set up shop right with you territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T00:29:22-07:00","id":129692,"title":"","content":"105) In a city with a high crime rate, two households - the spirit courts of violence and madness - fight. Their conflict will soon escalate into the Flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T02:28:05-07:00","id":129743,"title":"","content":"106: A local official has found out about the People. He's not interested in killing or revealing anything, but instead sees an opportunity. The man has ambitions, and what's worse has the intelligence to see the golden goose in front of him. So long as the packs under his aegis do as they're told, he won't slip their names to any Federal authorities. Some packs have been willing to play ball, but the local Pure will have none of it. The enemy you know, or the enemy who knows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T09:45:51-07:00","id":135433,"title":"","content":"107) A wolfblooded ally approaches the pack. He believes that his daughter will very soon have her First Change.<br /> <br /> Problem is, they had a fight and she hasn't been around for a couple days. And she was last seen talking to a few known Firetouched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T09:48:18-07:00","id":135445,"title":"","content":"108) A missing werewolf member of an allied pack turns up in the Shadow - as a Ziir, devoid of any Harmony, cradling the skull of one of her victims.<br /> <br /> Kill her, or bring her back to her pack? Can she still be saved?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T09:49:40-07:00","id":135446,"title":"","content":"109) The ancestor spirit of a proud, strong line of werewolves approaches the pack. He says he wants the pack to redeem his werewolf family - the pack used to be Forsaken, but its members have defected to the Pure years ago. The ancestor spirit would very much like to assist the PCs in bringing the pack back to Luna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T08:20:35-07:00","id":136761,"title":"","content":"110) The PC's are getting on in years and soon it may be time for them to retire and become mentors for the next generation. They have all produced children who have undergone the first change and are ready to take up their parents' legacy. So what will the elder pack do when they find out their children have joined up with the Bale Hounds, secretly biding their time until their parents were too old (and presumably weak) to stop their defection?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-14-2014, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T09:36:23-07:00","id":140617,"title":"","content":"111) A very experienced Half Moon has gained notoriety for her beliefs about the Shadow and the Forsaken condition.<br /> <br /> According to her, the fact that the spirits prefer to work with the Pure and against the Forsaken isn't written in stone. Given some hard work and a few concessions, the Forsaken might well convince powerful spirits to lend the Forsaken their support.<br /> <br /> Not every spirit needs to be hunted down if it violates the rules. And rules can be guidelines, right?<br /> <br /> Purists among the Forsaken detest the Elodoth's laissez-faire style of dealing with the spirit world (it's a slippery slope, they say ...); but that doesn't change the fact that she's has better, stronger spirit allies, and the Pure generally leave her be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T12:27:41-07:00","id":140818,"title":"","content":"112) The Fire-Touched have always been fanatical zealots, but their latest alpha has gone straight off the deep end. She offers the local Forsaken an ultimatum, either join her tribe and be purified, or she and her fanatics will go begin massacring humans in the streets. They have until the next full moon to agree to her terms, which is thankfully a month away. Its a race against time to locate the Fire-Touched lodge and stamp out this rampage before it starts!<br /> <br /> <br /> 113) The PC's are all newly changed werewolves and don't know much about their responsibilities. The bad part is before they came along, the Forsaken and Pure were deadlocked in power against each other, and a brand new pack could be just what they need to tip the scales in their favor. At first both tribes seem to be friendly enough in offering them membership, but when the players start taking too long to decide, things turn ugly. Their latest recruitment ploy was pretty straight forward &quot;If we can't have you, we'll make sure they can't either!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T21:43:55-07:00","id":146358,"title":"","content":"114: There's strange lights in the sky, and for once you're paying attention. The Rat Host have been active more in your territory, and things have been escaping. The most pervasive spirits around your territory are those of what most people would consider aliens, UFOs, and flying saucers. Just one of the joys being so close to Wright-Patterson Air Force Base. If the rats are inside the base itself, that means trying to get inside and rooting them out, and dealing with the fallout of the still-roaming spirits that thinks like an alien being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T20:45:17-07:00","id":149107,"title":"","content":"115) For well over 20 years now, the city has had problems with pollution and illegal dumping and it's gotten so bad it's starting to produce a haze in the air. Unnaturally black clouds hang over the city, obscuring the sunlight and respiratory illnesses are becoming more common and the city is strangely reluctant to clean up its act. As the resident pack of Iron Masters, the PC's are shocked when the look up to see the cloud of smog has a face, and it's leering down upon them. This cloud isn't a cloud, it's a colossal spirit of poison, and it's growing powerful enough to manifest itself in the physical world!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T09:21:26-07:00","id":157929,"title":"","content":".) .) One of the most skilled, experienced Lodge of Prophet Cahaliths has seen the PC's imminent death in her dreams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T05:44:00-07:00","id":160740,"title":"","content":"117: There's rumors another reality show modeled on the, &quot;Slightly creepy morally upright family has dozens of spawn&quot; angle in your area, and you don't like who they're filming. They're a Fire-Touched wolf-blooded family, and the filmmakers don't realize that they're about to give the family, and by extension the Pure, a frightening new recruiting tool to drag innocent people into being their new slaves. It's clear; shut down filming, and kill this show before it lifts off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T00:34:23-07:00","id":169553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daydreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/11952-1001-werewolf-story-hooks?p=14343#post14343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">58) Lunacy stops working.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, given how nWoD works in general, I don't see this changing much.<br /> <br /> 118: Through your regular patrol of your territory, you hear the distance sounds of wood pummeling against flesh quickly followed by a wet smack. you come to the source of the disturbance to find a body of a person near dead while the nearby tree spirits spits out insults of the most colorful sort. You drag the unconscious form back into the material. Judging by the fact the wounds aren't rapidly healing, you take this person for a human. As the person starts to rouse, he/she begins to babble about being &quot;cursed&quot; and gives a description of a nearby Lune and frequently changes shape into wolf and back before falling back into slumber. Could a Lune curse a person into a different kind of werewolf instead of Uratha? And if so, how will the news affect the rest of the Uratha packs nearby?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T19:51:53-07:00","id":201729,"title":"","content":"119: This... Isn't normal. This isn't normal at all. See the local Hisil has gone... domesticated. The Murder spirits? Have started hosting Mystery novel clubs. A couple of pain spirits have made a cargo cult of an office building, complete with trust building excercises. A tree spirit and a computer spirit have gotten maried! One of them is visibly pregnant! The thing is, they've also stopped causing trouble, and have become positively polite to the Forsaken they see. Your pack is going to have to figure out what's going on.. And is it really worth stopping?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T03:31:49-07:00","id":201938,"title":"","content":"120) The waitress is a real looker. &quot;Would you like to have fries with that?&quot; she asks. &quot;By the way, you should really stop this stupid chase. Leave town, maybe.&quot; She gives you her best smile as she continues: &quot;and don't bother following this body after work. Alice..&quot; - she points at her name tag - &quot;..will be dead in the morning, and I'll be using a different body next time I talk to you.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T19:05:32-07:00","id":202545,"title":"","content":"121) The PC's are being followed by flaming wolf heads that float about in the air. They don't speak or appear hostile, they just follow around staring at them expectantly. No humans else can see them, so apparently they're spiritual in nature. What the hell do they want? Because the line is drawn at watching you go to the bathroom!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T12:03:10-08:00","id":312464,"title":"","content":"123) The mad moon decides it's time to awaken the wolf in someone. There's a First Change, and the PCs get to play babysitter for a new Forsaken werewolf. <br /> <br /> Problem is, the young cub doesn't just have problems adjusting to Forsaken life - most young wolves do - she also can't deal with her auspice. She's the reluctant killer, he's the shaman who's frightened by the very idea of the Shadow, she's the judge afraid to pronounce judgement. The very idea of his auspice offends the new werewolf. <br /> <br /> It's up to the PCs to help him come to term with the destiny Luna has chosen for him; if they don't want him to end up with the Pure or at the feet of the Maeljin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T13:12:59-07:00","id":650478,"title":"","content":"124) A fetish of unimaginable power, possessed by a god of fear, will arrive in the city very soon. Everyone knows it already - every Cahalith within miles has had nightmares in which the fetish featured prominently. <br /> <br /> Obviously, pretty much everyone in the know about these things will try to steal the fetish. Wolves. Spiders. Rats. Leeches. People with powers. Simply everyone. <br /> <br /> Twist: the spirit-god inhabiting the fetish has methods of controlling its user, making him his puppet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T11:56:33-07:00","id":654210,"title":"","content":"125) The pack encounters another pack that behaves in bizarre ways. They spend almost all their time in the <i>Hisil</i>, claim to serve an entity called &quot;Gaia&quot;, and have an inexplicable beef with some tech startup called &quot;Pentex&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T08:08:55-07:00","id":655164,"title":"","content":"126) The PCs are hired by members of another pack to babysit their children, who all went through the first change young and were put into a pack (which holds the school they go to and the shopping mall down the block from said school as their territory, plus their parents territory) together by their parents, while the parents are off handling a crisis (possibly created by the pups) in the <i>hisil</i>. The pups are that particular combination of smart and bored that leads to act out in spectacular ways, such as pranks on other supernaturals, which should be fun for the sitters...<br /> <br /> (because adventures in pup sitting needs to be a thing)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 09-07-2015, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T23:01:30-07:00","id":686576,"title":"","content":"127) Luna is somewhere down here in the projects. <br /> You heard me, man. Our crazy mother goddess. Down here. In mortal form. <br /> <br /> I've heard stories of our people meeting her - always in a different form, and none of us has met her more often than once. But she's around. <br /> <br /> There's this one blooded girl she asked if she wanted to be a warrior, prophet, judge, shaman or hunter. Well, the girl picked shaman, and she had her First Change as a crescent moon only a few days after. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T23:11:39-07:00","id":686579,"title":"","content":"128) A pretty powerful Crescent Moon without pack makes it a habit of killing people in a ritual manner and leaving their bodies for the authorities to find. <br /> <br /> The PCs might not approve. Upon asked, the Ithaeur (who doesn't appear to be all sane) will state that the killings are absolutely necessary in order to keep an insanely powerful spirit/demon/god/thing away. <br /> <br /> Now, the pack shouldn't have any real problem stopping the werewolf serial killer, but if they do so, they'll very soon start getting really, really bad nightmares of something getting through the Gauntlet and wreaking havoc on the mortal world - that is, if they don't offer any sacrifices. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T22:44:50-07:00","id":687955,"title":"","content":"129) A pack of werewolves with bizarre, machine-themed Gifts has cropped up, and has been proselytizing wildly about a &quot;God-Machine&quot;, claiming its superiority over even Mother Luna. Worse yet, their bizarre gifts show that that may actually be true.<br /> <br /> 130) A Werewolf has been blessed by Helios for the first time since the Urfarah's death, resulting in an Uratha of the Selenelion Auspice, changing at a Lunar eclipse with the Sun still visible in the sky. All the local Packs have been courting her to join them, and lead them toward final victory in the war against the Pure, as prophesied by Ithauer sages.<br /> <br /> 131) The recent Blood Moon Eclipse has produced a fearful Gishtahu/Surrarahu hybrid, possessing the wiles of the Eclipse and the cannibalistic madness of the Blood Moon. If he's not caught and subdued, he could caus incalculable damage to the local spirit ecology.<br /> <br /> 132) Your Pack stumbles upon a place where there is no gauntlet, the very last Border March. It seems like a fantastical, beautiful place, until a massive, beating heart is found at its center. The heart incites Rage in Werewolves. Some claim that it's the heart of the Ur-Farah. Is it? And if it is, what should be done with it?<br /> <br /> 133) Somehow, a Wolf-blooded in your Pack has Changed...but not into a Werewolf. He was instead chosen by Helios, becoming a being of flesh and fire. Will he remain loyal to the pack? And why would Helios decide to emulate his sister Luna?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T15:01:39-08:00","id":747500,"title":"","content":"Crossover hook with Requiem....<br /> <br /> 134) A Storm Lord from a neighboring pack has been found dead after disappearing on a lone hunt. An investigation reveals that a relative or close friend of his had been Claimed by an insidious yellow-eyed spirit of smoke and shadows, who used him to commit a series of still-unsolved murders. Unfortunately, things soon go from bad to worse. Several similar spirits are sighted in the area, Claiming more people to carry out a ruthless campaign of killings that leave widespread panic in their wake, it's enough to bring together all of the Uratha in a Siskur-Dah. But just as the packs completed the rite and move to carry out the Hunt, they suddenly find themselves attacked by a hit squad of Kindred whose leaders are convinced they're in league with the spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T18:31:27-08:00","id":805669,"title":"","content":"inspired by recent events in Oregon<br /> <br /> 135). Your territory has become the site of a standoff between a radical group and the federal government. The radicals are disturbing the local shadow and the increased attention being paid to the area is hampering the pack's ability to hunt, but killing the terrorists isn't an option due to the amount of attention being paid to the standoff by various news sites. The news reports make it clear the radicals don't know what they are doing, have no intention of leaving and seem to want a battle with the feds (As long as the feds shoot first so that they look like the bad guys), maybe this calls for a more subtle approach...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T22:57:30-08:00","id":805824,"title":"","content":"136) There has been a sudden rise in wanton acts of destruction throughout the protectorate, but you and your pack are as clueless as every other werewolf in the city. The fact that the evidence points to a powerful spirit of destruction doesn't help when none of the spirits in the Hisil deny any involvement. And as the incidents continue to rise in frequency, the packs may have a lead when they hear word of a man claiming to be on a quest for the monster responsible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T05:32:53-08:00","id":805999,"title":"","content":"137) Whispers travel across the protectorate of a &quot;former&quot; werewolf. If you believe what they say, he was a wolf one day, a normal human the next. When asked, he claimed that he was &quot;purified by a spirit of humanity&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T21:57:25-08:00","id":807602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/11952-1001-werewolf-story-hooks?p=805999#post805999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">137) Whispers travel across the protectorate of a &quot;former&quot; werewolf. If you believe what they say, he was a wolf one day, a normal human the next. When asked, he claimed that he was &quot;purified by a spirit of humanity&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tie-in to 137 for a possible crossover with Mummy. And a shout-out to <i>Lore of the Deceived.</i> <hr /><br /> 138) There is more - and less - to this claim, however. And the suspicions of several werewolves are confirmed when the former werewolf is attacked by a monstrous undead creature and its cult of human followers. While one of the local packs managed to drive them off, they know it's only the beginning upon hearing the monster claim that the man stole a relic that was 'rightfully his'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T11:34:52-08:00","id":808085,"title":"","content":"139) Crossover hook for mage...<br /> A Firespeaker elder appear out of the blue during a meeting between the local Forsaken packs. He claims that Pangaea was lost not by farther wolf's death but by creatures known as the Exarch's. He offers absolument for the Forsaken's sin against father wolf, if they are willing to fight along side the pure against the Seers. Is this a trap, a trick for disposable troops in some war the pure has gotten themselves into. Or could this be what reunite The People.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10820,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","user":"Blakemikizuki","date":". 01-20-2016, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T08:19:08-08:00","id":814140,"title":"","content":"140) Human scientists show calculations that are an evidence of solar system having 9th planet. So called Planet X circles it on a very large, elliptical orbit. Last time it appeared closest to us was 15 000 years ago, before humans started to make tribes and form first civillizations. Now it's slowly coming towards Earth again. Maybe that's why we have perfect half-moon for third day now...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.sciencemag.org/news/2016/01/feature-astronomers-say-neptune-sized-planet-lurks-unseen-solar-system\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.sciencemag.org/news/2016/...n-solar-system</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7871-miriander","name":"Miriander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T01:27:22-08:00","id":817469,"title":"","content":"141) There is something strange going through a local Hisil. nature spirits are moving back on masse and the artificial ones are providing a way less resistance than they should. New, strange magath are appearing made of the merger of natural and artificial spirits and they don't seem as insane as their brethren.even the landscape is changing into a phantasmagorial merger. With the spirits being strangely tight-lipped, or ignorant, the only lead is a sighing of a pair of spirits in the hisil, one looks like an old style angel and the second as a man made of steel and plants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T02:04:35-08:00","id":817472,"title":"","content":"142) There is a new pack in the town. However, they are very strange. None of them has any marks, or signs that they have been removed. Instead a strange golden script runs in thin bands all over them. None of their gifts is known to any werewolf in the vicinity and their totem is... strange. Spirits reported that they worship a strange stone tablet with a single rune in their loci.<br /> <br /> 143) A well known ghost wolf had disappeared in a shadow and was presumed dead till a week ago. Now he claims to have been cured from the moon madness and indeed is much calmer and collected then other werewolves. The other point? His wolf forms have changed, strips of rainbow scales run through the fur like a demented form of luna's brands and a set of heavy antlers sprouts from his head. And what is this talk of the rulers of life and spirit he is proselytizing about?<br /> <br /> 144) Someone had built a fortress in Hisil. It's not a spirit reflection of the real world, it's a genuine building erected directly in the shadow. Overnight. <br /> A strange barrier bans both spirits and werewolves from entering it. Just when both were going to get their act together and figure out what that thing was a host of minor spirits rose from it, all carrying the same message:<br /> &quot;The Shadow Amphitheatre is open! Come, watch, fight and win!<br /> Fights to death, fights to win! Shadow Chess and Mage Duels on weekends!<br /> entrance fee 1 Essence, participation fee 5 essence, Prize - 100 Essence for day's winners!&quot;<br /> *Resonance and Essence spill are taken care off. No freeloaders.<br /> <br /> 145) A strange priest has taken a sway over the neighboring pack. He promises deliverance from rage and madness. The werewolves following him indeed seem a Lot calmer and controlled. They also react and deal with any trouble on their territory with incredible speed. But, why are their marks warped so strangely? What are those new strange moon gods and spirits they have taken to honoring? and why some spirits claim to have met strange silvery apparitions that no werewolf can see?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T12:42:16-07:00","id":848347,"title":"","content":"146) A new dance craze has taken over the city's youth culture. This dance, which is kind of like a stripper's take on the macarena mixed with a <b>very</b> sexually suggestive twirling motion but performed by two dancers instead of one, normally wouldn't rate on the Uratha's radar except some of the lyrics seem to be in first tongue and a pack you know in LA says that one of the record producers involved is a member of that, cult the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/809400-umaraha-e-the-children-of-the-worm\">Umaraha'e</a> that has been causing so much trouble lately. Add in the fact that teenage Uratha who perform the dance seem to be going mad and mutating into hideous forms make it obvious that the hit song &quot;Black Spiral&quot; needs to be suppressed before it creates a bigger problem.<br /> <br /> 147) the movie industry has recently moved into the protectorate's area in a big way, as a result of tax credits the regional government put in place. As a result, the local spirit politics have been disrupted by the arrival representatives of Ilthum related to Hollywood who have overthrown the old spirit court and established the Court of the American Dream Factory. This normally wouldn't be a problem, the protectorate found that the old spirit court was... frustrating, to the least. The problem comes from the fact that the three humans that have the biggest stake in this, a studio executive, a producer and a Chinese diplomat, are well known for being behind some of Hollywood's worst trends (read any of cracked.com's articles on Hollywood business practices and Chinese influence over the industry for ideas). The result is that the hisil has become a commercialized mockery of itself, with the last straw being when the local Cahalith started getting ill-fitting product placements in their prophetic dreams.<br /> <br /> Looks like someone's going to have to save the shadow, but how is the protectorate supposed to take on an entire industry <b>and </b>a foreign government?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 03-17-2016, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T19:20:17-07:00","id":856169,"title":"","content":"148) The wolf-blooded child of one of your pack members has been replaced by an imposter. They look right, they act right, they know things only they should know. But you can tell they're fake, they don't smell like a wolfblood. When the pack investigates further, they'll notice the imposter has a stalker, <i>one who </i>looks <i>oddly familiar</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T21:27:57-07:00","id":856234,"title":"","content":"149) The local Ghost Wolves have been banding together and withdrawing from the wider Forsaken community. Nobody is sure exactly what's caught their eye, but willworkers gave started to go missing and the spirits whispers praise to Eater of Names, the lost Firstborn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T21:50:35-07:00","id":900679,"title":"","content":"150) The players hear rumors in the Shadow about a mortal in a nearby territory. Suposedly they bear no touch of Wolf or Moon, but the Spirits have actually begun to worship them, converting simply from being in this person's presence. They've attempted to do anything they can to earn their idol's approval, alien mindsets and insane zeal mixing into a number of disasters the pack that runs that area has attempted to cover up. And the most disturbing part? After encountering the other pack in person, the PCs realize that the half-Spirit children of Wolf and Moon are merely resistant to this bewitchment. Already, the other pack has become violently territorial and willing to do anything to protect their &quot;precious&quot;...<br /> 150B) As above, but the other pack is <i>Pure</i>, a mostly Fire-Touched group that have convinced themselves that this person is their messiah, who they're planing to kidnap so they can &quot;educate&quot; them as to their &quot;destiny&quot;. Will the PCs be able to save this person without being aflicted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T21:56:16-07:00","id":900682,"title":"","content":"<b>151)</b> It was almost undetectable at first. The world's population of rats began to decline, first subtly and then quite rapidly. Within a matter of months, any rat that wasn't already in a cage had seemingly vanished off the face of the planet. The humans were preparing to investigate the phenomenon, and that's when everything went to shit. An explosion of spiritual essence, several times larger than anything you've ever heard of, right in the heart of United States of America.<br /> <br /> Every physical entity within 200 miles was stricken with leprosy on the spot, unleashing a plague that caused withering and decay in all it touched. Even the great Storm Lords are bristling their fur in realization of what is to come. The Plague King has been reincarnated... and this time, there's no Father Wolf to put him down!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T06:38:07-07:00","id":900894,"title":"","content":"152) Your pack was sent to the quiet coastal town of Rockport, a stone's throw from Corpus Christi, to investigate the disappearance of an elder wolf's cousin and their pack. Everything seems pretty calm, until one night, you are attacked by some kind of shark-man. It claims to be an envoy of the furious sea god Tethys, demanding blood payment for the oil spilled into the seas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T14:18:39-07:00","id":914364,"title":"","content":"153) Your pack was lucked to come across this newly-Changed guy or gal before they managed to cause too much trouble. They're a bit out of it (okay, a <i>lot</i> out of it) but, to be fair, so were you when you walked in his shoes. Except there's something funny about them; the way they walk, and talk, and what they talk about, you'd think they were native to the Shadow. Which is crazy talk, of course; everyone knows that Spirits can't become Uratha! ...Well, at least that's what you've always been <i>told.</i> But whatever the case, at least this person's just an isolated incident, right?<br /> <br /> ...<i><b>Crap.</b></i><br /> <br /> [Inspired by conversations in another thread. Basically, Spirits resonant with the concepts associated with the People become capable of undergoing the First Change for no understandable reason. What the heck is going on?]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T18:55:42-07:00","id":938495,"title":"","content":"154) A local criminal crew has been robbing the front businesses of werewolf packs in the city. It started off with a group of stores (a Chinese restaurant, a 7-11, a clothing store aimed at stupid teenagers with too much money and a wine shop) owned by the Heirs of T'ai Djin pack and then escalated until eventually a bank that laundered money for the local ivory claws got hit by the gang. The local hunters appear to be just as confused as you are and the leeches and witches seem be victims of these guys as well, which raises the question... how are these guys pulling these heists off?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 07-27-2016, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T08:38:09-08:00","id":1012602,"title":"","content":"155) For some reason, the pack has gained the loyalty of a dog/wolf spirit. That's great, friendly spirits are always in shortage, but this spirit is a magath (it's tainted with technology, or wound-essence). As a dog(or wolf)spirit, it is loyal to the pack, but its mere presence agitates the local spirits, enough to cause a severe strain to the packs spirit relations. What should they do with their unconventional ally? Do they leave it be, perhaps threaten the local courts to accept it? What will happen when other uratha in the area learn that the pack's been rubbing shoulders with wound-spirits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Dam da namsithim.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12696-lost-his-mind","name":"Lost-His-Mind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12696_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T20:53:22-07:00","id":1076789,"title":"","content":"156.) A female Uratha of (insert tribe here, But I would like to do this with an Iron Master and Red Wolf is the father ) is pregnant and claims the father is her tribe's firstborn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 04-11-2017, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T23:32:27-07:00","id":1076826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/11952-1001-werewolf-story-hooks?p=856234#post856234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">149) The local Ghost Wolves have been banding together and withdrawing from the wider Forsaken community. Nobody is sure exactly what's caught their eye, but willworkers gave started to go missing and the spirits whispers praise to Eater of Names, the lost Firstborn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally missed this plot hook.<br /> <br /> If you happen to be running it, feel free to give my Eaters of Names Lodge a look.<br /> <br /> ---=---<br /> <br /> 157) The existence of the Nameless Wolves has been the stuff of rumors for Pure and Forsaken alike. Yet as a Mage works to hunt them down for their souls, local Uratha with allegiances to both find themselves forced to work together when members of the fabled Lodge appear to assist... for a price.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-14-2017, 04:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T06:46:09-07:00","id":1077694,"title":"","content":"158) The Unchained are not unknown to the People, but they tend to avoid deliberately tampering with each others' affairs. But then a pack on the outskirts of the protectorate dropped out of contact, and were later found in the service of a Tempter. They're serving it willingly, and they claim that the Demon has figured out how to create Gifts and carve them into Werewolves. Are they legit? And what could this mean for the protectorate and wolf-kind at large?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T20:33:20-07:00","id":1112480,"title":"","content":"159) Turns out some of those artifacts that Hobby Lobby got busted for smuggling were parts of Bau's Teppe Magath. It's the Forsaken VS the Long Night VS ISIS in.....<a href=\"https://www.inverse.com/article/33824-hobby-lobby-fund-isis-meme\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters </a><a href=\"https://www.inverse.com/article/33824-hobby-lobby-fund-isis-meme\" target=\"_blank\">of the Lost Hobby Lobby</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 07-06-2017, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T07:52:30-07:00","id":1112676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/11952-1001-werewolf-story-hooks?p=1112480#post1112480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">159) Turns out some of those artifacts that Hobby Lobby got busted for smuggling were parts of Bau's Teppe Magath. It's the Forsaken VS the Long Night VS ISIS in.....<a href=\"https://www.inverse.com/article/33824-hobby-lobby-fund-isis-meme\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters </a><a href=\"https://www.inverse.com/article/33824-hobby-lobby-fund-isis-meme\" target=\"_blank\">of the Lost Hobby Lobby</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Damn you for making me want that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T15:08:59-07:00","id":1112946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/11952-1001-werewolf-story-hooks?p=1077694#post1077694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">158) ...But then a pack on the outskirts of the protectorate dropped out of contact, and were later found in the service of a Tempter. They're serving it willingly, and they claim that the Demon has figured out how to create Gifts and carve them into Werewolves. Are they legit? And what could this mean for the protectorate and wolf-kind at large?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would mean they are Bale Hounds or at very least be considered as such by other Uratha. Most likely both if they admit to it. I am pretty sure they won't appreciate the nuanced difference between a Vice spirit and/or Vice spirit-claimed and a demon, except they might see the demon as worse because they have a harder time affecting it. Sound like a fun adventure to tempt the PCs on and have them choose between being brutal monsters that slay evil or brutal monsters that serve evil, or possible some other gritty dark choice. <br /> <br /> <b>160) </b>A <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1002118#post1002118\">stern beautiful Norse-looking woman</a>, whom has been said to fly through the air, has been murdering Uratha with near impunity with a silver spear of all things. A couple packs claim to have killed her but later she's back without a scratch and whichever members of the offending pack that advocated dealing with her are violently murdered, either then or eventually. This is story is shared with you by a wild-eyed and tearful Cahalith from the far coast of the continent who is begging to join your pack for protection, because they confess to be hunted by this woman for speaking out against her. The Cahalith hasn't slept, washed, or eaten in days and is quite pitiful. Does the Cahalith deserve help or to be put down for bringing such a being to your city?<br /> <br /> (This version of Nemesis Replaces Stutter Step with Hunter's Sense: Those with the Transgressed Condition, And her Surprise Entrance power only works in scenes with those with the Transgressed Condition), carries a Silver Spear +3L instead of a Dagger, which reforms with her as if it were part of her, and lastly She has Staff 5 Covering these skills Drive, Larceny, Socialize, Streetwise, and Persuasion representing the pool of those that had the Transgressed Condition looking to absolve their Guilty condition as well. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Transgressed (Persistent)</b></span><br /> <b>Effects:</b> You have Transgressed against a Nemesis and are marked for punishment. You can feel the weight of your sin upon you like a lead blanket, and feel the dread of something is coming to punish you. This feeling begins as soon as you get this condition and lasts until you don't have it anymore. You are a valid target of her Surprise Entrance and Hunter's Sense Dread Powers. Also gain Embarrassing Secret or Notorious Condition depending on whether this Transgression is known as those that know of your mark will treat you differently. <br /> <b>Cause:</b> Opening the Doors of others to act against the Nemesis, attempting to use hard leverage against the Nemesis, deliberately causing any type of injury to the Nemesis. Any of the previous against the Nemesis' s patron.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Sincerely confess your guilt to the Nemesis, beg for forgiveness and accept the Guilty and Broken conditions if she forgives you through her Doors being opened only through soft leverage. Die at the hands of the Nemesis. <br /> <b>Beats:</b> The Nemesis uses Surprise Entrance to enter a scene you are in.<br /> <br /> Note: Concessions to alleviate the Guilty Condition are requested in the form of bringing others whom have Transgressed to the Nemesis. <br /> <br /> STORYTELLING TIP: The reason Uratha have yet to be spared is the trend to pridefully attack or attempt to intimidate threats and how unlikely they are to sincerely confess and beg for forgiveness. In this matter mortals have a great advantage over Uratha, they know their frailty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-07-2017, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:43:09-07:00","id":1117326,"title":"","content":"<b>161)</b> One of your wealthy and influential wolf-blooded Pack member has met the man of her dreams! He's articulate, brilliant, confident, competent, kind, and an expert in everything she cares about. She met him on an exclusive <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1117279#post1117279\">dating site which guarantees</a> results, and in her head and heart she's already planning the wedding. She was feeling deeply lonely and depressed without stable romantic options because of her being a member of the pack and her high pressure job. She is asking how she should introduce the PCs to her potential future husband, and it is obvious she is in love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-18-2017, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T20:24:38-07:00","id":1118042,"title":"","content":"162) a pure pack has bought your protectorate's local tv station and is spinning the local news to blame various local problems on the area's forsaken packs, influence the hisil and benefit their own interests in general. How will you take them off the air?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T20:45:42-07:00","id":1118051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/11952-1001-werewolf-story-hooks?p=1117326#post1117326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>161)</b> One of your wealthy and influential wolf-blooded Pack member has met the man of her dreams! He's articulate, brilliant, confident, competent, kind, and an expert in everything she cares about. She met him on an exclusive <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1117279#post1117279\">dating site which guarantees</a> results, and in her head and heart she's already planning the wedding. She was feeling deeply lonely and depressed without stable romantic options because of her being a member of the pack and her high pressure job. She is asking how she should introduce the PCs to her potential future husband, and it is obvious she is in love.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 163) While tracking down Ideal Inc. by following the bloody trail their Ideal Mates leave (the first drop of blood having come from your pack), you eventually find ones that have &quot;stabilized,&quot; so to speak. They show no emotional instability and suffer no violent fits of rage, but instead show little quirks and odd behaviors. Turns out that they're all Ridden by spirits antithetical to the Resonances created by the Ideal Mates, as a means of protecting their own feeding grounds. Furthermore, it appears that possessing these clones is much more easier for spirits in general, according to the Ridden clones. While the choice of leaving the Ridden be or hunting them down is an obvious issue, there's one more problem. The Shadow is yet unaware of this advantage, given the lack of Ridden clones. Ideal Inc. also seems oblivious, given the lack of spiritual defenses on their &quot;products.&quot; With every Ideal Mate on the loose, a mass outbreak of Ridden and Claimed becomes closer and closer, and they're not going to be so docile as the already Ridden ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T10:46:44-07:00","id":1124375,"title":"","content":"<b>164) </b>A god-like Dihar (Rank 6) that appears as a giant serpent with bloodily severed wings, which reeks of deception and secret knowledge, dwells in a Place-That-Isn't connected to a major political buildings within easy travel of the pack's territory, and has sent an envoy to the Pack. It is requesting that the Pack's Ithaeur bind its Master into a Fetish at its Master's behest and is offering unlimited access to the Place-That-Isn't in exchange. The Place-That-Isn't has passages leading to many arcane, occult, and political locations around the world, and contains hints of some secret society clandestinely controlling <i>Everything</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1124179-2e-bale-hounds-fetishes?p=1124358#post1124358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Fetish Flaw Condition</span></b><br /> <b>Breached</b><br /> The fetish does not perfectly contain the entity within, there are cracks in its prison that it can exploit. A bit of its Influence and Manifestations insidiously sips out during its use.<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Effect:</b> The user gains the Resonant Condition appropriate to the Entity bound within the fetish when they use it and don't already have that Condition. The condition lasts for a day. If they do have that Resonant Condition it becomes Open for a scene, and if already Open the user gains the Persistent Urged Condition which redefines the Urge each time they use it. After having earning 15 - (the contained Entity's Rank) worth of Beats from that Condition they gain the Possessed Condition for a scene each day afterward. This continues to happen unless the body of the victim is destroyed (it'll continue to happen to corpses after death), the Possessed Condition gets ended via Abjuration, exorcisms and forced contact with banes or bans while it is happening, or the victim is Claimed. If the victim goes a year being subjected to Possessed Condition each day the victim gains the Claimed Condition caused by the entity within and the Fetish disintegrates as it escapes, and everyone affected by this fetish flaw are freed from cycles of gaining the Possessed Condition.<br /> <b>Cause: </b>Dramatic Failure in Fetish Creation; Apparently &quot;succeeding&quot; Fetish Creation on Entities greater and 5 Ranks;<br /> <b>Beats: </b>Are awarded for the conditions this causes.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Unbeknownst to the pack the Dihar has discovered the above loophole that would allow it to Claim a body in the Material world without diminishing its strength. As far as the supposed secret society, it may be a Mystery Cult Initiation with Seers of the Throne and other powerful beings forming a cosmos spanning conspiracy... or maybe its a ploy... possibly both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 08-03-2017, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T16:44:58-07:00","id":1146484,"title":"","content":"165) <a href=\"http://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/2017/09/25/wolves-discovered-living-just-outside-rome-first-time-century/\" target=\"_blank\">Wild wolves have returned to Rome</a>, and thus the ancient feud between Saturi and Marisi is reignited over the newly arrived Urhanu and wereblooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T04:16:36-07:00","id":1146962,"title":"","content":"166) A local elder discovers that his mother is one of the Pure Ones, she is still alive and actively hunts Forsaken with her pack, he himself cannot check that rumor because his high Primal Urge keeps him away from human populated territories. The Pack must track her down and capture her alive, if they manage to kill her pack and bring back trophies, even better.<br /> <br /> 167) 10 years ago the local packs managed to kill a reptilian god-like entity that is rummored to originate from within the Gauntet, 10 years later carnivore dinosaurs of alien shapes (flying T-rex) started devouring great prey populations driving the local packs hungry. Smaller sized beasts have been tracked down to local farms feasting on cattle and humans alike. The pack is sent to the place where the repltilian deity was killed to investigate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T10:25:43-08:00","id":1173031,"title":"","content":"<b>168)</b> A <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171004-ten-spirits-binded\">Spirit Noble</a> of Rock (&amp; Roll) and their retinue has entered your Pack's territory on Tour. Their presence is throwing the local Court's politics and stability into chaos and attracting all manner of unruly interlopers. Will the Pack:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Try to fight off this Baron of Metal and Shadow?</li> <li>Strike a deal with the new Spirits?</li> <li>Use the local chaos to their advantage?</li> <li>Challenge the intruding Spirit to a guitar battle?</li> <li>Exploit the influx of concert goers for money and influence?</li> <li>Lie low and pick up the pieces once this blows over?</li> <li>[Other]?</li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T14:19:42-08:00","id":1173083,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>, whole idea of 168 sounds a lot like this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yVm8C6RdcDM\" data-code=\"yVm8C6RdcDM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/yVm8C6RdcDM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T15:11:57-08:00","id":1173096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/11952-1001-werewolf-story-hooks?p=1173083#post1173083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>, whole idea of 168 sounds a lot like this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yVm8C6RdcDM\" data-code=\"yVm8C6RdcDM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/yVm8C6RdcDM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>(So what if I've been playing it recently...)<br /> <br /> There are worse combinations that Werewolves and Heavy Metal, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T17:27:09-08:00","id":1182752,"title":"","content":"169) Mysterious, semi-tangible creatures have begun to appear, simply manifesting wherever humanity has created the conditions for them to manifest, whatever those actually may be. Solid and visible to a few, but completely unnoticed to most of the herd. These beings, called Serpents by the mortals aware of them, but often resembling lizards due to the highly variable number of limbs, resemble living organisms, yet defy many basic laws of nature or physics. Possessing no digestive, nervous, reproductive, circulatory or skeletal systems, the exact mechanics of how they work are left a mystery. What is clear, is that the Serpents live exclusively in urban areas, predominantly manifesting near or inside especially large buildings, favoring the tallest structures in the area. Though some breeds favor underground tunnels.<br /> <br /> Some Serpents have hides made of leather, skin, or scale, some have flesh of wrought iron, plastic, or paper. Many are completely hollow inside, others are filled with rare gases, motor oil, human organ tissue, or other, seemingly meaningless substances. While exclusively found on the flesh side of the gauntlet, their existence and behaviors are oddly spirit like, each 'breed' devoted to a single act, chewing wires, clogging gas tanks, inducing stutters, luring people to deserted areas to mangling them beyond recognition... They are mostly disinterested in humans, outside of how they might factor into their compulsions, or whatever bans or banes the things may have, if they have any at all.<br /> <br /> Where did these so-called 'Serpents' come from, why have these creatures begun to infest the herd's cities, and how can the pack deal with the effects they may have on their territory?<br /> <br /> ((OOC note; This is actually something I've been thinking of, on and off, for quite some time. Originally built out of an obscure reference, I've been mulling over a minor template focused on the concept, and how it might optionally tie into most major splats. Not sure if I'll ever turn my notes into genuine home-brew, though.))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":2598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","user":"Gryphon's Feather","date":". 02-05-2018, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T08:39:57-07:00","id":1213069,"title":"","content":"170) Something has riled up a bunch of ghosts on a marshland near a nature preserve just outside the packs' territory. The reserve was claimed by a pack of Hunters in Darkness, but they've gone dark. The ghosts are capable of animating marshland and brackish water to zombies, but they're so weak that they surely weren't the demise of the Hunter-pack. What happened?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Dam da namsithim.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12696-lost-his-mind","name":"Lost-His-Mind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12696_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T10:56:09-07:00","id":1213485,"title":"","content":"171) A heavy metal concert on pack turf is getting swarmed with spirits of negative feelings. The band in question is dressed up like GWAR and they sound like (link below). Something about them is clearly calling spirits to their concerts, with the latest actually resulting in a riot and several Ridden. The band has been touring pretty much all over the state, but they're so high-profile that even a pack with no Storm Lords can see that some of the bandmembers are not wearing costumes. Why have they been left alone? Should the pack intervene? And how?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://sothoth.bandcamp.com/releases\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://sothoth.bandcamp.com/releases\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://sothoth.bandcamp.com/releases\" target=\"_blank\"> https://sothoth.bandcamp.com/releases </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Dam da namsithim.","edited":{"userid":12696,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12696-lost-his-mind","user":"Lost-His-Mind","date":". 04-30-2018, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12696-lost-his-mind","name":"Lost-His-Mind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12696_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T03:20:31-07:00","id":1213720,"title":"","content":"172) Multiple protectorates around the world find their attention falling upon the Lodge of the Lost as it finds itself at risk of collapse. Many of its eldest and most powerful adherents are being inexplicably twisted into Empty Wolves, each similar to the rest in that they manifest serpentine traits as they change. These <i>Urusum</i> (as they come to be called) are beasts of hunger and rage, and the Uratha who scramble to hunt them down may find that they only represent the beginning of the problem.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> This is a tie-in to LostLight's Hirt Isfet, the Convergence mechanics I contributed, and the conspiracy's history/hostility towards the Lodge of the Lost for their folly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T11:13:14-07:00","id":1213832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryphon's Feather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/11952-1001-werewolf-story-hooks?p=1182752#post1182752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">169) Mysterious, semi-tangible creatures have begun to appear, simply manifesting wherever humanity has created the conditions for them to manifest, whatever those actually may be. Solid and visible to a few, but completely unnoticed to most of the herd. These beings, called Serpents by the mortals aware of them, but often resembling lizards due to the highly variable number of limbs, resemble living organisms, yet defy many basic laws of nature or physics. Possessing no digestive, nervous, reproductive, circulatory or skeletal systems, the exact mechanics of how they work are left a mystery. What is clear, is that the Serpents live exclusively in urban areas, predominantly manifesting near or inside especially large buildings, favoring the tallest structures in the area. Though some breeds favor underground tunnels.<br /> <br /> Some Serpents have hides made of leather, skin, or scale, some have flesh of wrought iron, plastic, or paper. Many are completely hollow inside, others are filled with rare gases, motor oil, human organ tissue, or other, seemingly meaningless substances. While exclusively found on the flesh side of the gauntlet, their existence and behaviors are oddly spirit like, each 'breed' devoted to a single act, chewing wires, clogging gas tanks, inducing stutters, luring people to deserted areas to mangling them beyond recognition... They are mostly disinterested in humans, outside of how they might factor into their compulsions, or whatever bans or banes the things may have, if they have any at all.<br /> <br /> Where did these so-called 'Serpents' come from, why have these creatures begun to infest the herd's cities, and how can the pack deal with the effects they may have on their territory?<br /> <br /> ((OOC note; This is actually something I've been thinking of, on and off, for quite some time. Originally built out of an obscure reference, I've been mulling over a minor template focused on the concept, and how it might optionally tie into most major splats. Not sure if I'll ever turn my notes into genuine home-brew, though.))</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, at least, these are clearly spirits belonging to the same, very strange Choir, perhaps emanating from a Place-That-is-Not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T12:16:34-07:00","id":1214722,"title":"","content":"<b>173) New Pangaea</b><br /> Something stirs inside the Gauntlet. Uratha and Spirits Reaching through it report a sense of movement and purpose. Belishu have been observed being repelled by forces emerging from where they gnaw, and Alzu are being evicted from their nests. Oracles and seers (cryptically) tell one thing - Pangaeans are returning/reforming.<br /> <b>A) </b>Fragments of the ancient ones are being reborn. Turtle rises once again. Bull's Heart beats once more in its chest. Echos of howls presage even the return of Wolf. But are these the same beings they were before, or new gods filling old roles?<br /> <b>B)</b> But these Pangaeans are not the old gods of elements, beasts, and cycles. They are new ones formed from Humanity's impact upon the world. How will the Uratha take Wolf being replaced by some aspect of the Herd?<br /> <b>C)</b> These Pangaeans are not as they were, however. They embody alien concepts and clashing natures. Some say that Idigam have usurped the role of the old gods.<br /> <b>D)</b> The Pangaeans are reforming, but the process is not complete. Powerful representatives of their old roles are competing to be the new embodiment of Fox, Spider, and Reflection. Which Uratha will win the title and become Wolf Reborn?<br /> <br /> [If you want to downgrade the cosmic implications, you could instead re-cast this as a local restoration of the Border Marches, with the Gauntlet remaining (for the moment) as it is everywhere else.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T05:45:26-07:00","id":1236732,"title":"","content":"<b>174)</b> Something has happened and the Wounds have ruptured the Gauntlet, turning <i>every</i> Wounded site into a locus/verge where Wounded Spirits are spilling out into the Gurihal. Some of the Herd are crying about it being the &quot;End Times&quot; and that this is Hell invading the Earth. The <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1234267-seeking-salvation-lodge-of-the-saviour-2e\">Lodge of the Savior</a> is trying to rally other Packs around them and lead an offensive, but get curiously cagey when asked about how such a thing could happen.<br /> <br /> [ST's can reduce the range of influence to a region, if they don't want to deal with worldwide consequences.]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"><b>YOU MANIACS! YOU BLEW IT UP! AH, <i>DAMN YOU! GOD DAMN YOU ALL TO HELL!!</i></b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-19-2018, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T00:03:21-07:00","id":1249633,"title":"","content":"<b>175</b>) A wolf-blooded, or human packmate is in trouble. Their company was doing things they weren't supposed to be doing and he found out. Now he's on a hit list. But it's not a thug that's going to come after him, it's a spirit. Can you protect your packmate? Can you do it while also finding out how this company can send spirits out to kill and whatever else they were doing?<br /> <br /> It can be made a ghost or other entity. Even a host. If ephemeral, spice it up so that it will only attempt to kill when the target is alone, requiring them to either use the target as bait, or babysit them.<br /> <br /> <b>176</b>) The trap worked, you trapped the host in and the fire went off and now they're surely dead. Except not quite. In the chaos, a hungry spirit of fire and death decided it's had it with the increased safety measures throughout town, and went and claimed one of those fleeing beshilu. His arson crusade was cut short, however, as he was eaten by another beshilu. A beshilu who's just gained Influence over Fire that will only increase in power and use it gets bigger. And since it has Warp Shard it can also start creating new ones like it.<br /> <br /> Feel free to change the host or spirit. Perhaps electrical azlu that craft a great web through the powerlines across the territory? Or just use other powers, one of my razilu has Beast's Dragonfire.<br /> <br /> <b>177) </b>That Ivory Claw pack has been a monument in town. Built around a family, between their wealth and connections they maintain a strong control over even the territories of Forsaken wolves. Yet aside from some 'punishments' for acting against them, and the disappearance of an entire pack that was trying to get other Forsaken to go after them, they seem content to let the Forsaken go about their business. But now a member of your pack receives a text or phone call. They claim to be one of the daughters of the Pack's patriarch. And she also claims that the Change will be coming over them soon and the family is going to ensure Luna's brands never appear on her. But she doesn't want any part of it, and asks your pack for help for her escape so that she can join one of the Forsaken tribes and be properly awakened to Luna.<br /> <br /> It might be a trap! Perhaps it's not, and it wasn't even she that contacted you, but a Lune or emissary from your tribal totem. Meaning you would have to take her unwillingly from a ritual she wants to do.<br /> <br /> <b>178) </b>You had to watch this guy. The lunes and spirits all agreed, he was going to have his First Change. And the Pure have been on a recruiting run lately so you needed to get to him before they did. And it begins, in suitably violent manner during an attempted carjacking. Criminals torn to bits. Better get your elodoth on that. But something weird happens when it wears off. In hishu form, he climbs off the ground, dusts himself off, looks around in a fearful manner, gets back into his car and drives off. Leaving his werewolf body behind. It also awakens, shifting from gauru to dalu. Somehow, his hishu form is out there on its own.<br /> <br /> Maybe he doesn't even have dalu, and the guy (or girl, all these can flip around) can't go to human or near-human. What's the human side doing? Is it aware what happened? How do you tell the werewolf that his life has changed and, apparently, ignored him and kept going.<br /> <br /> <b>179)</b> Babysitting again. He's supposed to have his First Change tonight and, fortunately, it looks like he's working late at his office in the middle of nowhere. Wait till it happens, try to minimize the damage without becoming a target, wait till he passes out, then explain things to him when he wakes up. Easy peasy you thought, until he kept raging after the first ten minutes. And now, the guy's been raging for 8 hours now and it doesn't look like he's going to stop. His office building is wrecked and it looks like he's going to make his way to more populated areas. To make matters worse, the sun is rising, work is starting soon and people will be coming back to the office. And he's still raging.<br /> <br /> <b>180)</b> A firefighter went through their First Change. He's a good guy, takes the Oath of the Moon seriously but refuses to join a tribe. He explains that, as he was raging, surrounded by fire, he saw and connected with something more vast than him. And after finding out about Uratha culture, he's decided it must be one of the firstborn, a fiery wolf that burns whatever it touches who is only rumored of in some of the most obscure of legends. Eventually, he comes to your pack, because he wants your help finding it and releasing it from its imprisonment or awakening it from its slumber.<br /> <br /> For a potential twist, maybe the legends also suggest that this firstborn would be staunchly on the Pure side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-29-2018, 03:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T05:36:50-07:00","id":1249671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/11952-1001-werewolf-story-hooks?p=1249633#post1249633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>180)</b> A firefighter went through their First Change. He's a good guy, takes the Oath of the Moon seriously but refuses to join a tribe. He explains that, as he was raging, surrounded by fire, he saw and connected with something more vast than him. And after finding out about Uratha culture, he's decided it must be one of the firstborn, a fiery wolf that burns whatever it touches who is only rumored of in some of the most obscure of legends. Eventually, he comes to your pack, because he wants your help finding it and releasing it from its imprisonment or awakening it from its slumber.<br /> <br /> For a potential twist, maybe the legends also suggest that this firstborn would be staunchly on the Pure side.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sutr-Ur, the Burning Wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-09T11:46:03-07:00","id":1259841,"title":"","content":"181) The pack receives a message. Prophetic dreams, a visit from an ithalunim, scrawled on a wall in their turf, you choose. But the message is next to (or follows a discovery of) a chunk of a gauru werewolf...<i>made entirely of silver.</i> The message in question is as follows:<br /> <b>Life becomes pain<br /> Pain becomes death<br /> Death becomes silver</b><br /> Sounds a lot like a group of mages got mad at a werewolf, but the theme could fit Silver Wolf and his Ivory Claws as well... Whose arm/leg/head is the chunk from? Is it going to happen again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Dam da namsithim.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12696-lost-his-mind","name":"Lost-His-Mind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12696_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T23:35:46-08:00","id":1274843,"title":"","content":"182)<br /> The spirits are gossiping about a relatively nearby Pure Pack losing an extremely powerful Loci to some unknown being. That Pure pack suffered greatly and there are rumors they suffered several casualties by terrible non-spirit monsters. Since they're Pure, the PCs have no direct lines of communication. Coincidentally about a week after the Pure situation stabilizes a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1269755#post1269755\">being which looks like a bearded balding Russian man</a> able to fulfill the aspirations of mortals has enter the PCs territory. This being calls himself Gregori Rasputin and has taken an interest in the mortal loved ones within the PC's pack. Rasputin first noticed one of the mortal members of the Pack with an Aspiration which would be unusual and reveal their alliance with supernatural forces. This observation took place where the pack member could have been seen by him &quot;People Watching&quot; with his <i>Knowing Gaze</i> Dread Power. Since being noticed that pack member has been followed by Rasputin's Acamoth familiar (Please note it is a Geotia, and not a Spirit thus not subject to powers which target Spirits, and is visible in the Astral frequency but not with Spirit frequency of Twilight) to find their social circles including the PCs, possibility other Packs, and the other mortal members of those pack.<br /> What does Rasputin want? To find mortals with Aspirations that he can twist in interpretation to bring Horrors from beyond the edge of reality into reality or transform people into such creatures. He is not afraid of werewolves, and has previous manipulated them into researching a how to enact Rusputin's Bane, which releases <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1272792#post1272792\">Anak'vog'soth</a> into the physical world. Even though that involves Rasputin's death at the hands of his Bane he doesn't fear that outcome, since he has contingencies for his Abyssal allies to resurrect him in that even. In fact that's what happened to the Pure's Loci. If Rasputin is confronted by the PCs, he'll likely be happy to bargain with them for leaving their pack and territory unmolested in exchange for favors like their assistance in murdering both Pentacle cabals and Seer pylons. It is possibly for the PCs to negotiate terms which even include Rasputin assisting them, if they don't mind assisting making the world a lovecraftian nightmare realm of chaos and madness. Of course that'd get other Uratha and Spirits to declare them Bale Hounds.<br /> <br /> 183)<br /> An incident of indiscreet slaughter of innocent people who were obstacles of a local pack of werewolves' Sacred Hunt (possibly the PC's pack if they are so callous and careless) has been the inciting bit of evidence and motivation for the founding of a mortal hunter cell. The Cell comprises of some members of the police officers that investigated the scene, a few medical examiners, and grieving family of those that died. Since publicly admitting the existence of the supernatural monsters would make them lose everything they still have left they have opted to clandestinely seek justice through investigating their weaknesses and enacting brutal violence. With investigative background, some tactical training, and a fully understanding they are hunting a supernatural group whom are more terrifying than anything they can imagine they've formed a healthy paranoia. From the evidence they have collected, they come to believe physics as they understand them don't apply to supernatural beings and these monsters could be capable of anything. At the minimum these hunters think what ever they hunt can disappear, reappear, shape-shift, tear apart people like rag dolls, and are literally immortal like a slashers from scary movies and have no idea what their weakness is. This makes these hunters supremely cautious because they intend to survive killing all the monsters they find, possibly leading to extreme overkill.<br /> <br /> 184)<br /> The cell of monster hunters above (story 183) is noticed by Rasputin (story 182), and he is absolution delighted by a young man named Kyle Owen who is the grieving son of one of those killed by werewolves. Kyle's Aspiration of &quot;Give my life to defend &lt;Insert town here&gt; against werewolves&quot; is perfect for Rasputin to twist in intention to transform Kyle into a Potency 5 Horror, and he has already convinced the impressionable lad he can grant such a boon. Kyle is expecting to die in the ritual as he believes he's the human sacrifice to power it, however instead Rasputin intends to transform Kyle into a soul devouring immortal abomination suited to completely depopulate the area of Uratha, allowing the local Spirit ecology to careening out of control and leaves Rasputin twist peoples desires to free if the PCs don't interrupt the ceremony then they'll have to deal with <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1274838#post1274838\">Kyle Owen</a>, and it is almost assured they'll lose their souls, and likely die in the attempt.<br /> <br /> 185)<br /> The players are the new Uratha in the area, and unbeknown to them the established Packs in the area back in their hayday successfully dealt <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1274838#post1274838\">Kyle Owen</a> (story 184) back in the 1950's. They have strict rules about being outside of city limits each full moon they expect the PCs to follow without question and not super-keen on explaining why. An obvious powder keg, and one the highly Renown Uratha will hold the PCs accountable for their disobedience, knowing full well to stay outside of the city limits, but not feeling the need to tell the PCs any hints on what to do, while simultaneously quite insistently demanding they &quot;deal with their mess&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 12-17-2018, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T03:58:10-07:00","id":1380346,"title":"","content":"186) An idigam has spirit-claimed someone. Idigam-Claimed. This one's gonna be a doozy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T03:58:50-07:00","id":1380347,"title":"","content":"187) A young woman turns up on one of your hunts, grows a glowing blade, &amp; manages to slay your foe.<br /> Turns out that she is the hybrid of human &amp; a full moon lune, &amp; she wants to join your pack &amp; aid in the performing of the job of Uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T03:59:32-07:00","id":1380348,"title":"","content":"188) Your pack has been approached by a Geryo, who considers you little brothers &amp; sisters &amp; has decided to join your pack. But it is clearly the most alpha in this group &amp; thus is the logical leader.<br /> How can you take of advantage of this? Is it possible to take advantage of this? Should you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T04:00:27-07:00","id":1380349,"title":"","content":"189) A very dangerous &amp; bizarre super-shartha has appeared out of nowhere. It is a mishmash hybrid of spider-host, rat-host, wolf-host, worm-host, fungus-host, locust-host, snake-host, crow-host, &amp; others.<br /> No one knows what it wants, but it is quickly apparent that it wields a very dangerous way of effecting the Gauntlet. Gauntlet Domination.<br /> Yes, the local Gauntlet bows to its very will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T04:01:02-07:00","id":1380350,"title":"","content":"190) So an old kindred, just out of torpor has made friends with a pack of Forsaken Uratha.<br /> See, they were definitely wolf-blooded in life &amp; naturally still have their Tell.<br /> The pack in question are wondering how take advantage of this very useful ally they've acquired, without making them decide there are better packs to ally with?<br /> Other werewolves, ones not of the pack in question, are asking themselves &quot;how do they respond to this upset in the normal balance between the local packs?&quot;<br /> With the vampires, well, this werewolf-friendly kindred is rather free with the information they have regarding kindred when talking to Uratha. So that's a problem that needs dealing with.<br /> Where do you stand? With any of the above, or a different group entirely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T04:02:17-07:00","id":1380351,"title":"","content":"191) So an old kindred, just out of torpor has made friends with a pack of Forsaken Uratha.<br /> See, they were definitely wolf-blooded in life &amp; naturally still have their Tell.<br /> The pack in question are wondering how take advantage of this very useful ally they've acquired, without making them decide there are better packs to ally with?<br /> Other werewolves, ones not of the pack in question, are asking themselves &quot;how do they respond to this upset in the normal balance between the local packs?&quot;<br /> With the vampires, well, this werewolf-friendly kindred is rather free with the information they have regarding kindred when talking to Uratha. So that's a problem that needs dealing with.<br /> Where do you stand? With any of the above, or a different group entirely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T04:03:15-07:00","id":1380352,"title":"","content":"192) A cult(?) of Lupus et Fidelis, the Church of the Wolf, has really pissed you off. Upon tracking them down &amp; them cowering under your unbridled wrath, it occurs to you that they might make for good subordinates/servants. You just gotta keep them believing you're gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T09:41:52-07:00","id":1380395,"title":"","content":"193)A rural Forsaken pack discover a mysterious area of &quot;broken time&quot;, filled with impossible spirits from times that never were or almost were. Strange structures, existing solely in Twilight, are also found, the doors barred by werewolf rites never before seen, using magics no Forsaken is familiar with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T10:08:13-07:00","id":1380408,"title":"","content":"194)A Bale Hound bodhisattva predator has emerged from nearly a century of dark meditation, and his flesh sizzles and pops as Essence wells up within him. His words distort spirits that hear him, and werewolves can be literally caught in the serene monster's shadow.<br /> <br /> He is preparing, you see. He has spent a hundred years cultivating s single Wound, slowly gnawing away at the Shafow of the area, preparing to bore a hole straight to whatever hell the Maeljin inhabit.<br /> <br /> Lunes are raving of this threat, and even the monstrous Pure totems seize up in fearful anticipation...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T14:09:11-07:00","id":1380474,"title":"","content":"195) A nascent Uratha is coming up to their First Change. Everything's in place, nothing could go wrong.<br /> The nascent wolf will undergo First Change, be contained, the world they are part of will be explained to them (after they've come done from the First Change bloodlust), &amp; then they will be returned to their human life with the added duty of what the wolves do.<br /> Then they enter First Change &amp; start turning into a spider creature (turns out they are Etummu not Uratha). This is different.<br /> <br /> \u2022 See the Etummu thread on RPG.net for information about Etummu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T14:10:29-07:00","id":1380475,"title":"","content":"196) The city's Cahaliths all experience simultaneous visions. Very vague ones. The only thing that anyone can tell for certain from the visions is that a new night club called Black Spiral, spells bad news for all Uratha. Unless if it turns out you're a Bale Hound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T14:11:48-07:00","id":1380477,"title":"","content":"197) The Beast of G\u00e9vaudan. A vicious, man-eating monster that terrorized the province of G\u00e9vaudan in the Margeride Mountains of south-central France between 1764 &amp; 1767.<br /> What is not as well known, even suppressed, is the fact that the Beast was an Uratha of an Auspice that had never been seen before &amp; hasn't been seen since. Until just last week when your little brother went through his First Change to that very Auspice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T14:12:53-07:00","id":1380478,"title":"","content":"198) The Beast of G\u00e9vaudan. A vicious, man-eating monster that terrorized the province of G\u00e9vaudan in the Margeride Mountains of south-central France between 1764 &amp; 1767.<br /> What is not as well known, even suppressed, is the fact that the Beast was an Uratha of an Auspice that had never been seen before &amp; hasn't been seen since.<br /> Modern-times. All is well. Until you hear that a local Cahalith has just had a rather disturbing vision. The Beast is coming back to life, &amp; it's using the body of one of your packmates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T14:15:05-07:00","id":1380480,"title":"","content":"199) One of the territories your pack's territory borders on belongs to a pack of three very personable &amp; easy to deal with Pure.<br /> The Ivory Claw believes in purity of motive, in being honest about why you're doing what you're doing. The local gangs, as well as some of the cops, politicians, &amp; etc., are keeping them occupied &amp; that doesn't look to change any time soon.<br /> The Fire-Touched preaches that people must know all sides to a story. Otherwise they can't make a proper choice about important decisions, like whether to be Forsaken or Pure, or which Tribe to join.<br /> The Predator King alpha of the pack states that one should never try to hold &amp; govern more than they're capable. They respect raw physical might &amp; if beaten will accept their defeat.<br /> The pack are good neighbours. They brought a roast boar to the last protectorate, smoothed relations with the dominant Shadow Noble, &amp; provided extra muscle when fighting the azlu half a year ago. The Fire-Touched gets regular requests to tell the myths, legends &amp; other stories of the various Uratha people be they Pure, Forsaken, Bale Hound, Ghost Wolf, or just possibly other.<br /> <br /> a) Then a wandering Forsaken pack comes into the area. They say that this arrangement is a blasphemy against Luna &amp; that the only good Pure, is a dead Pure.<br /> Do you ally with your fellow Forsaken, with the personable Pure pack, or will you try &amp; stay out of this conflict letting it resolve on it's own? At the end of the day, where do your loyalties lie?<br /> <br /> b) Then a large number of Pure pack comes into the area, talking about doing a pogrom against any &quot;false&quot; Pure. The local Pure pack is declared to be &quot;false&quot; &amp; there's going to be a very public execution in the next couple of days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T14:16:55-07:00","id":1380481,"title":"","content":"200) You've come across one of the strangest magaths that you have ever seen. It glows with the golden light of the sun. It glows with the silver light of the moon. It is a magath of the sun &amp; the moon, &amp; it cannot reconcile the two sides of its nature.<br /> It has come to a solution to fix this. The spirit court of the sun &amp; the spirit court of the moon will bury the hatchet, forgive &amp; forget. It just needs a bit of help getting the two groups sitting at the table...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T14:17:27-07:00","id":1380482,"title":"","content":"201) We have confirmation. Every child born at this hospital within the last two weeks, has been wolf-blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T14:20:11-07:00","id":1380484,"title":"","content":"202) For a long time there has been turmoil between two kindred. So long that each of them has had sufficient time to go into &amp; come out of torpor. The reason for the conflict has been lost (&amp; possibly the fog of ages).<br /> These two kindred each have vast resources including human servants, a personal ghoul family, powerful connections in kindred, mundane, &amp; other supernaturals societies. Each owns a small country &amp; has majority shares in a mundane corporate business.<br /> Except now, for reasons beyond your understanding, the two of them want to bury the hatchet. They have decided to mark this peace treaty with a marriage between a scion from each ghoul family. But they require people to guard the bride &amp; groom to be from any parties who might desire to sabotage this truce.<br /> Oh, &amp; despite the fact that the prospective husband &amp; wife are going along with the wedding doesn't mean they support it. They themselves hate the idea of burying the hatchet &amp; intend to sabotage the wedding as much they can, without defying their respective vampire lords'.<br /> Your pack or werewolves have lucked out, &amp; are the only people in at least a thousand miles who can a) do the job &amp; b) have zero loyalty to any of the parties involved. Refusal is not an option.<br /> <br /> Note: trigger warnings on the two plot hooks in my next post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T14:21:48-07:00","id":1380485,"title":"","content":"203) Your elderly, human grandparent has started being influenced by a spirit of depression &amp; is contemplating suicide.<br /> <br /> 204) The most powerful spirit in town is one embodying white supremacy.<br /> None of your pack are white.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T14:23:10-07:00","id":1380486,"title":"","content":"205) Every Cahalith in the city has had the same vision. An idigam coming down from the north. A geryo coming up from the south.<br /> Because no one wants such a thing to be true, scouts were sent out.<br /> The visions are true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T14:27:18-07:00","id":1380487,"title":"","content":"206) Your pack is made up of a bunch of Uratha that every other pack in the area decided would be more trouble than they were worth.<br /> There's a genuinely pacifistic Rahu who's an atrocious tactician. An Irraka whose sense of honour demands they never use stealth. An Ithaeur who's atrocious at talking to spirits &amp; can't craft a fetish to save their life. A Cahalith who calls their visions &quot;lies sent by the Devil&quot; &amp; is terrible at being a lorekeeper. And finally an antisocial Elodoth who always finds a way to come across as extremely biased in their judgements.<br /> The pack has noticed some great threat on the horizon. If it gets where it's going there will be devastation like nothing seen before. No one else has noticed this oncoming threat &amp; no one will believe you when you try to tell them about it.<br /> It's, unfortunately, up to you to stop this all by yourselves. Good luck, you'll need it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","user":"Krat05","date":"the storytelling of the Cahalith when this first went up. Sorry. 05-03-2020, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T16:19:20-07:00","id":1380512,"title":"","content":"207) Your pack finds its way into a small, out-of-the-way, rural town.<br /> The inhabitants of the town pray to Father Wolf, Mother Moon &amp; their children. They have an extensive &amp; incredibly accurate (as much as it can be) collection of stories of their &quot;gods&quot;.<br /> However, lunes are coming, intent on correcting the town's religion. If corrections are not possible then a purging will be called for.<br /> And there you are, caught in the middle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T19:36:52-07:00","id":1380554,"title":"","content":"208) The cat-shifters known as the Colony have declared war upon your pack.<br /> When asked why they draw attention to a series of human sacrifices the pack has performed in the last couple of weeks, &amp; provide hard proof.<br /> Your pack has no recollection of committing such crimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T19:37:27-07:00","id":1380555,"title":"","content":"209) You're one of the Forsaken &amp; have no idea who your birth parents are. You desire to find out. You discover that one of them is an anshega, &amp; the other is a Baal-Hadad.<br /> Yes, they're both still alive. And you're investigating your heritage has made them aware to the (maybe continued) existence of their child.<br /> They are coming to say hello. Both of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T10:19:48-07:00","id":1380693,"title":"","content":"210)The players' characters have discovered a door in their house that wasn't there, the night before, a dull black door that is locked tight with silver locks, silver hinges and silver reinforcements. On nights of the full moon, bizarre, horrifying noises can be heard coming from the other side of the door.<br /> <br /> When they finally get the door open, it reveals a passageway into the Shadow Realm---to be specific, a Place-That-Isn't. This Place-That-Isn't is a nightmarish reflection of the pack's dwelling, and the place is inhabited by distorted spirit-reflections of the players' characters.<br /> <br /> What in the hell is going on?!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T14:46:47-07:00","id":1380771,"title":"","content":"211) Any Uratha going through their First Changes in a city, within the last couple of months, are turning into animals other than wolves.<br /> They're Uratha in just about every way, except for the part where they turn into wolves. Animals forms seem to be random &amp; without coherency.<br /> <br /> [Personally this seems a bit garbled on another read. Each person going through First Change turns into an animal. That animal is now their beast side.<br /> The other interpretation (&amp; the one I didn't have in mind when coming up with this plot hook) of this is that every time one of these new Uratha assumes a form other than human, they &quot;draw&quot; a random animal.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T14:47:33-07:00","id":1380772,"title":"","content":"212) Ordinary people have started going into murderous rages, apparently at the drop of a hat.<br /> Then someone realizes the rages can all be attributed to a weird infection found in the murderous people's bodies.<br /> Then an Uratha realizes why the murderous rage looks so familiar. Kuruth has become contagious &amp; is going through the human population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T14:48:10-07:00","id":1380773,"title":"","content":"213) A fellow Uratha pack in the area has gotten a new totem spirit. Something happened to the old one &amp; they needed a new one.<br /> The new spirit unsettles you. It's dark, hateful looking, has suspect goals for a pack totem.<br /> When asked from which spirit court it comes, it answers &quot;the Abyss&quot;. Now what does that mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T15:48:14-07:00","id":1380781,"title":"","content":"214)The players' characters find strange creatures unlike anything seen before stealing mortals and taking them to a Place-That-Isn't unlike they've ever seen before. It is a hedge-maze that never ends, with bizarre entities fueled by nonsensical drives and the power of inviolate promises. Can the players' character track the mortal down, before his captor brings him to the mysterious &quot;old gods of thistle&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T10:58:10-07:00","id":1381022,"title":"","content":"215)The situation is dire, as a Ghost Wolf tyrant and her cult has allied with the cult of some 'dying-and-rising-again-and-again' undead horror. <br /> <br /> The Ghost Wolf tyrant and the undead proto-Egyptian monstrosity have become lovers. Using forbidden Gifts taught by spirits of cancer, the Ghost Wolf tyrant...has become <i>pregnant</i> with her undead paramour's baby.<br /> <br /> As time goes by, as the birth draws near, the players' characters' Cahalith receives a vision: this child will be a FULLY MATERIAL magath, PERMANENTLY in the physical world!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T19:30:27-07:00","id":1381184,"title":"","content":"216)In a ruined ghost town in rural [Fill-In-The-Blank], in an abandoned arts school, kids have been gathering to dance, listen to very loud music and smoke quite a bit of herb.<br /> <br /> Then..,they all disappearad. ALL OF THEM, including a Wolf-Blooded cousin of one of the players' characters. Naturally, the pack investigates.<br /> <br /> The indurate pavane had taken them all, and now the dancer has emerged from its chrysalis...just in time for the players' characters to arrive!<br /> <br /> (Thanks to the awesome Chris Allen for the creepy-as-frick indurate pavane!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 04-14-2020, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T03:40:25-07:00","id":1384143,"title":"","content":"217) The Counciliators Methodology of the Talbot Group has had a major victory. The Talbot Group as a whole has agreed to try &amp; use the &quot;wolf-people&quot; they have to help with encounters with spirits.<br /> You're part of the first attempt at this. You are either one of the &quot;wolf-people&quot; that the Talbot Group has picked up, or you're a member of the Talbot Group itself.<br /> The higher-ups just one thing to say: don't screw this up.<br /> \u25cf Uses the Talbot Group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T03:44:54-07:00","id":1384148,"title":"","content":"218) A Les Myst\u00e8res cell has concluded that the physical world &amp; the spirit world should not be so seperate from each other.<br /> The spirits should be able to come in &amp; move through us to keep the world healthy. After all, the spirits only hurt people who deserve it, right?<br /> The cell has decided that, in light of this &quot;truth&quot; they should help facilitate the passage.<br /> To this end they have allied with a swarm of beshilu. Between themselves &amp; the rats, they should be able to punch a proper hole right through the barrier seperating the two, &amp; have it be a permanent one.<br /> \u25cf Uses Les Myst\u00e8res.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T03:46:03-07:00","id":1384150,"title":"","content":"219) Your pack got attacked by some kind of vicious, lupine spirit-monster. When you retaliated, your Gifts acted as if the beast wasn't there. You managed to get away in one piece, but you were unable to kill the monster.<br /> Now you've got to find something that can hurt it &amp; hunt it down, because it's attacking every Uratha it comes across, uncaring about allegiance.<br /> \u25cf This is my attempt at porting the unihar to 2e. Way I figure it, unihar are not simply created when two Uratha mate, though that does have some bearing on the creation of one of these monsters. I have decided that there is some curse attached to a few rare lineages of Uratha. When an Uratha with the curse mates with another Uratha, the result is an unihar, gender has no bearing on the situation. Wolf-blooded can have the curse, but they are more carriers of it more than anything else, it sits in them dormant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T03:47:05-07:00","id":1384151,"title":"","content":"220) You wouldn't have believed it were it not for rock-hard proof shoved right under your nose. Two towns, practically neighbours to each other, each ruled by a Ghost Wolf Tyrant.<br /> Searching for new vassals to be used in the war between themselves, they have looked towards your territory. They see lots of capable servants there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T03:48:11-07:00","id":1384154,"title":"","content":"221) Seeking a wolf god to personally serve, a group of Lupus et Fidelis have managed to find a Ghost Wolf Tyrant.<br /> The Church of the Wolf have spoken of the wolf's divine nature to them, &amp; the tyrant has started to believe it, &amp; has also started engaging in certain practices that the gods of old once did.<br /> Recently it decided to find itself a &quot;spouse&quot; for at least a few seconds. It was drawn to one of your wolf-blooded relatives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T03:48:42-07:00","id":1384155,"title":"","content":"222) A pack of considerable influence &amp; might has cultivated a two or three of the cicada host.<br /> Earlier in the week, the cicada hosts were released into the wild (albeit with leashes on) &amp; then drawn back to their &quot;nest&quot;.<br /> When asked why they did this, the pack said: &quot;to draw in every shartha in such-&amp;-such radius, &amp; wipe them out in one fell swoop&quot;.<br /> The plan itself is bad enough, but this time is just a test. If it works good enough, then the pack will start doing it more often.<br /> Oh, &amp; apparently there's several packs all ready to follow in this one's footsteps, all with their own cicada hosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T03:49:36-07:00","id":1384156,"title":"","content":"223) A potent locus has been found in the relative wilderness. The only thing to get past is a survivalist militia-style cult that have made their fortress there, &amp; won't just leave.<br /> You make plans to make them leave through brute force.<br /> You put the plan into motion.<br /> The militia respond by pulling out guns (which was expected), &amp; some of them took Gauru form (which was not expected).<br /> What the Hell? You could have sworn they were human!<br /> \u25cf Uses the Army of Fenris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T03:50:28-07:00","id":1384157,"title":"","content":"224) Uratha (Pure, Forsaken, &amp; any other factions) tend to consider the high school you attend as a sort of training ground for young Uratha. That's all well &amp; good.<br /> The problem is that the three most alpha Uratha are leaving in a couple of weeks (graduation, moving away, fired, whatever works), leaving at the top of the food chain a young, particularly divisive Pure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T03:51:16-07:00","id":1384158,"title":"","content":"225) On a recent hunt, you encountered a hunter that seems to be a bit odd.<br /> After performing rigorous yet subtle tests, you have determined the origin of the oddness. They literally have an idigam bound to their blood.<br /> Then they come to you in a panicked state. Apparently they know of your nature as a werewolf. Crap how'd that happen? You can't have let it slip during that first meeting, right? Anyway, they say that a large, growing group of their kin are coming. They need you to deal with this. <br /> You would say no, except you're rather curious as to what has caused this great panicked state.<br /> \u25cf Uses Hrt Isfet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T03:52:01-07:00","id":1384159,"title":"","content":"226) Your pack came upon a group of people on heavy drugs, naturally surrounded by spirits of recreational drugs.<br /> You got rid of the spirits, for now, &amp; got these people sober to discover that they were veritable spirit magnets. They will find spirits againagain or spirits will find them, that's just inevitable.<br /> Now, how do you take advantage of this &amp; should you?<br /> \u25cf Uses the Illuminated Brotherhood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T03:52:37-07:00","id":1384160,"title":"","content":"227) An azlu uses one half of a married couple to elevate to azarath level. A beshilu uses the other half of the married couple to elevate to rokhan level at effectively the same time.<br /> Normally, the two creatures would try a kill each other, but the love their victims held for each other survived the transformation &amp; has overwhelmed other instincts, leaving the two monsters in an arguably loving relationship, though they don't particularly like each other &amp; fight all the time.<br /> To further complicate things, the couple were also parents &amp; the monstrous shartha have also inherited the protective, parental feelings their victims had.<br /> How can this be fixed? What are Hosts plans? And what are the child(ren) thinking &amp; feeling in all this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T03:56:38-07:00","id":1384161,"title":"","content":"228) A shartha hybrid unlike any other. Made by mixing a single member of a Adarusharu pack with an innocent human. The two are distinct creatures that now occupy the same space, changing in the times when day becomes night or night becomes day. The two are starting to bleed into one another, &amp; have started being able to assume a hybrid form.<br /> <br /> To &quot;up the ante&quot; (I think that's the right phrase), here are some possibilities: <br /> \u25cf You're not dealing with one of these hybrids, you're dealing with a whole fucking pack of them.<br /> \u25cf A number of regular Adarusharu have started to gather around the hybrid, recognizing them in part as one of their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T22:03:28-07:00","id":1385351,"title":"","content":"229) The Void Come to Earth. It claims to be a spirit come from the vast emptiness of space. Or maybe from another planetary body. Perhaps it was a void leviathan once upon a time. In any case, it crashed here long ago &amp; has come to consider the terrestrial Shadow its home.<br /> This mighty spirit arrives at a meeting of the local protectorate &amp; declares that it wishes to forge a Forsaken Lodge that has the spirits of the void beyond as its Sacred Prey. But it doesn't know how to go about this &amp; requests the assistance of any Forsaken willing to provide it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T15:36:08-07:00","id":1386188,"title":"","content":"230) Holes are appearing in the Gauntlet. Massive, growing holes spreading out from a large apartment building. You go in, ready to fight beshilu because they're obviously what you face here. You searched the building from head to toe looking for beshilu, &amp; didn't find a single rat. What you did find is an azarath whose fangs drip with venom that poisons the Gauntlet, causing it to wither &amp; die. Unfortunately, you managed to spook the monster &amp; it scarpered. Not to worry, evidence suggests that it's still in the region.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T15:37:20-07:00","id":1386189,"title":"","content":"231) &quot;Urfarah's successor comes!&quot; These words reverberate throughout the region's packs, stirring up conflicting emotions but one thing is for certain, you will be there to see this &quot;successor&quot; arrive.<br /> Soon it does. You see what an elder Uratha names as Lul'Aya. Several packs bend their knees in loyalty to this monster. It tells its new servants to prove their loyalty by killing the nonbelievers.<br /> \u25cf The attending packs &amp; wolves should be a mixture of Forsaken, Ghost, &amp; Pure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T03:51:29-07:00","id":1387234,"title":"","content":"232) One of the Firstborn has somehow accidentally impregnated a human woman, &amp; now needs a trustworthy pack to make sure the child lives to reach adulthood.<br /> The conception was consensual, &amp; one way or another the woman knew exactly what she was having sex with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T03:51:59-07:00","id":1387236,"title":"","content":"233) You're in the middle of the initiation into the Tribe of your choice when you are attacked by the sacred prey of your chosen Tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T02:31:48-07:00","id":1387439,"title":"","content":"234) Investigating the dissapearence of people, you discover a pack of Pure their totem being a powerful Mandragora Spirit, demanding human blood poured to it's roots. The territory of this pack includes a mandragora garden grown by a powerful Gangrel/Acolyte witch, master of Animalism and Cruac.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T01:26:12-07:00","id":1391439,"title":"","content":"235) A recently changed Uratha turns out to also be one of the most fanatical Christian priests in town, &amp; is very charismatic.<br /> They believe that werewolves are by nature demonspawn, &amp; that any that refuses to accept God in their heart is inherently damned &amp; must be killed now before they can hurt any good Christian souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T01:26:43-07:00","id":1391440,"title":"","content":"236) One of the Maeljin has been manipulating a certain local a bit more than normal.<br /> What will you do when you find out it's planning to use this person to become a Spirit-Claimed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T11:09:20-07:00","id":1399320,"title":"","content":"237)<b>The Door to Hell</b><br /> An Uratha pack discover a strange brass door in a Place-That-Isn't, in the Shadow Realm. The Place-That-Isn't itself is a seemingly endless series of office building hallways lot of fluorescent lighting, with stairs that go nowhere, elevators that all end in the same place and a sensation of absolute tedium. This Place-That-Isn't is itself only accessible by carefully searching a certain so-called haunted house in [Fill-in-the-Blank's] projects.<br /> <br /> Barred by powerful rites, getting the brass door open is a quest in and of itself. No other entities exist in this strangely silent Place-That-Isn't and, upon finally opening the door, one finds a stone labyrinth, open-aired, under a fractured yellow sky lit by two burning suns.<br /> <br /> Passing into this labyrinth removes the pack from reality as they understand it, leading them a realm they have no lore of. Though the walls have no roof, no matter how high one goes one can never actually crest the top. Imagery of weeping, kneeling figures abound, and strange &quot;Stonepunk&quot; machine-spirits linger here and there, speaking some alien tongue and performing bizarre, repetitive tasks.<br /> <br /> By solving the Labyrinth, the pack comes to its center to discover a stairwell made of stone heading down...into some unknowable darkness. Scenes depicted the Maeljin decorate the stairwell's walls, celebrating in bas relief the atrocities these devil-gods rebel in.<br /> <br /> The pack has found the door to Hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T00:22:41-07:00","id":1399528,"title":"","content":"<b>238)</b> A poor ethnic neighborhood suddenly has birthrates just completely stop. Any pregnant women whom live or even travel through it miscarry. It seems the like a combination of lack of use of contraceptives and charitably well-funded local Planned Parenthood providing free abortions for that particular area due to the donations of special interest groups has caused a the dumpster to become a Death Loci with a particular resonance. The Loci and the practices at the clinic have been feeding a small court of bloody-skittering-piles-of-crusted-fetus appearing death spirit feeding on the essence of children dying in the womb and the natural postpartum depression. That spirit court has hit critical mass so that they are proactively causing the miscarriages in order to reap more essence of their particular flavor. Given the delicate nature of life in the womb it isn't hard for the spirits to disrupt the pregnancy and cause the miscarriage. If left alone surely something more horrific will happen, either Claimed fetus corpses or Claimed Abortion Doctors, or attract larger less specialized Death Spirits. And even if the loci and all the spirits are destroyed the continuing practice will just reconstitute the same type of loci and spirits again, How does one deal with something like this without standing in the way of the woman's right to choose?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T18:26:44-07:00","id":1400225,"title":"","content":"230.<b>The Sculptor of Enamel</b><br /> The Beshilu of [Fill-In-The-Blank] rant and rave, for a &quot;messiah&quot; has come! A thing of lumpen flesh and jagged teeth with an umbilicus leading off to infinity, this toothy abomination is now in the area. She )for it is, at least nominally, female) seeks to create children, but in a womb of enamel, wrenched from the mouths of the dead and dying.<br /> <br /> The Beshilu crowd around her worshipping her as a messiah sent by unknowably mad blind idiot gods, and they have gone on a crazed rampage gathering teeth for &quot;mother&quot;.<br /> <br /> What will the pack do, when one of their Wolf-Blooded relatives have every tooth ripped out, and, with a mouthful of blood, raves about a toothy goddess?<br /> <br /> [Aa you might suspect, this is based directly off an insanely cool monster created by Mr. Chris Allan. Thanks, good sir!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T07:02:08-07:00","id":1400303,"title":"","content":"231) There is a huge uproar among the Spirit Courts. Something has awakened on the night-side of the planet. It claims to be the First Shadow, a creature of of immeasurable age, witness of both the Beginning and the End of Pangaea. It claims to have been an associate of Father Wolf Himself, who, it claims, charged it with a certain mission.<br /> <br /> It calls on uratha and spirit alike, who favor the shadows and darkness. Uratha that answer it's call are given a choice of either eyes or voice (It's a trick, choosing either joins the uratha into the lodge of this spirit).<br /> <br /> Choosing 'eyes', the spirit gently shuts the urathas' eyes and they become blind for a year and a day.<br /> Choosing 'voice', the spirit gently presses a fingerlike tendril onto the urathas' lips and they become unable to speak any louder than a whisper for a year and a day.<br /> <br /> Who knows why, maybe it has something to do with the &quot;mission.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Dam da namsithim.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12696-lost-his-mind","name":"Lost-His-Mind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12696_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T10:06:46-07:00","id":1402619,"title":"","content":"232)<b>Corporate Raiders</b><br /> The fine folks behind the HAST/'Ur' project have decided to test several new teratomorph designs, and choose the players' area as the perfect test-bed---with the intent of capturing the pack and using them as raw materials!<br /> <br /> (Thanks to Mr. Chris Allan, for the wonderfully gory HAST/'Ur' material!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T20:28:41-07:00","id":1414870,"title":"","content":"232) The United States Space Force is moving towards getting a proper base set up on the moon, for some unknown reason.<br /> There are still idigams trapped on the moon's surface.<br /> This could be a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T02:58:31-07:00","id":1414889,"title":"","content":"233: Hunters always have it out for werewolves, but one group really has a hard on. They run around carrying fetishes that don't use spirits, a witch contact called them &quot;relics&quot;. The People have no legends about them, but they seem to have legends about werewolves. Specifically, that they helped bring down Atlantis! Of course, that's bullshit (As far as you know) but they're in town and they're causing trouble. The spirits are in flux, and these idiots aren't helping. So what's your solution? The local Pure, who would just as soon eat you as look at you? The witches, who you've been jockeying against for essence? Or the local hunters, who you've been feuding with for over a decade? Pick fast, because these &quot;Greeks&quot; have backup...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T11:22:57-07:00","id":1448338,"title":"","content":"234) A lone Hunter in Darkness collapses just inside the pack's turf. He's running from a small mob of Azlu, who have already managed to poison him. He claims to have been able to permanently kill almost a dozen pursuers. Before dying, he hands an amulet to the pack. It's a a large piece of amber with a spider trapped inside. It's easily recognized as a fetish, but further inspection reveals that the spirit bound within is Azlu. What does the fetish do? Where did he find it? And what should the pack do with the growing mob of spider hosts skirting their territory?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Dam da namsithim.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12696-lost-his-mind","name":"Lost-His-Mind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12696_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T11:05:17-07:00","id":1451149,"title":"","content":"235)The grave of Father Wolf has been found! Located in a Wound of epic proportions and guarded by mad, blind Geryo encrusted in fungus-spirits, the gravesite stands above a subterranean pit leading.....somewhere unknown.<br /> <br /> Here, in an eternal sandstorm, jackal and hyena headed Maeltinets hunt anything that moves, while, in the Western distance, vast, decaying pillars stand like mute sentinels.<br /> <br /> A vast, skeletal wolf-thing, only vaguely lupine in nature, wanders here. The Maeltinets scatter before it in terror. If it sees Uratha, anger overcomes it. YOU ARE NO LONGER MINE, it proclaims, in a voice like thunder. BEGONE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 06-06-2021, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T09:04:10-07:00","id":1452962,"title":"","content":"236) It's night in the late summer of 1979. The news give out warnings of a strange astral phenomena, and recommend citizens not to watch it with the naked eye. The night is filled with screams. Some harrowing, some reverent, but all of them piercing and constant.<br /> <br /> Cahalith and Ithaeur characters have vivid and gripping nightmares of the moon cracking open like an egg, and something poking itself out for just a fraction of a second before waking up. Uratha watching the moon at night see a bright, full moon, and feel a wrongness, but can't really place where the feeling comes from.<br /> <br /> The Lunar Choirs are in absolute chaos. Those who don't attack other spirits and Uratha, seem to be fading away, or going into hiding.<br /> <br /> What happened? Is something wrong with Amahan Iduth? Did the Pure feel this too? Are they responsible?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Dam da namsithim.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12696-lost-his-mind","name":"Lost-His-Mind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12696_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T07:52:07-07:00","id":1453038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lost-His-Mind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/11952-1001-werewolf-story-hooks?p=1452962#post1452962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">236) It's night in the late summer of 1979. The news give out warnings of a strange astral phenomena, and recommend citizens not to watch it with the naked eye. The night is filled with screams. Some harrowing, some reverent, but all of them piercing and constant.<br /> <br /> Cahalith and Ithaeur characters have vivid and gripping nightmares of the moon cracking open like an egg, and something poking itself out for just a fraction of a second before waking up. Uratha watching the moon at night see a bright, full moon, and feel a wrongness, but can't really place where the feeling comes from.<br /> <br /> The Lunar Choirs are in absolute chaos. Those who don't attack other spirits and Uratha, seem to be fading away, or going into hiding.<br /> <br /> What happened? Is something wrong with Amahan Iduth? Did the Pure feel this too? Are they responsible?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this is inspired by something, but I can't remember the name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T08:06:05-07:00","id":1453364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/11952-1001-werewolf-story-hooks?p=1453038#post1453038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like this is inspired by something, but I can't remember the name.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I stumbled across the Local58 youtube channel recently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Dam da namsithim.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12696-lost-his-mind","name":"Lost-His-Mind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12696_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T15:20:59-07:00","id":1462937,"title":"","content":"<b>237/)Down Among the Dead Men</b><br /> A Hive-Claimed juggernaut prowls the countryside, smashing mortals to death with hammer-like hands of granite and gravedirt. It\u2019s giant form resembles nearly a dozen human corpses melded through as if through a combination of acid and surgery, and it\u2019s hump back is actually a bevy of smashed gravestones. It pounds it\u2019s victims to pulp, then smears the viscera on itself as it howls our wordless devotion to the distant star Vega and the horrid court of Void spirits that cluster around it in the night sky.<br /> <br /> It is a mad fusion of reanimated human corpses, spirits of gravestones, murder and, most disturbingly of all, things from the Deep Shadow. From the fissures in its body emits a sick green glow, and whispering can be heard <i>everywhere</i> near it.<br /> <br /> Now, it come to be accompanied by strange bird shapeshifters, corpse-eating things themselves who hear the mad cries from Vega the Hive-Claimed does. This alliance has set the local Shadow to panic. Can the PCs\u2019 pack stop this unholy alliance before it spills out of control?<br /> <br /> Note:<br /> Many thanks to Chris Allen for his awesome Orphean werebirds writeup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T10:32:04-07:00","id":1463113,"title":"","content":"<b>238/)Paint The Walls Red</b><br /> Beshilu have come to [Fill-In-The-Blank] masquerading a new congregation to the church they bought on the outskirts of town. They\u2019re very exclusive and publicly preach an extreme Christian creed while privately <i>preparing</i> for the gods they <i>TRULY</i> pray to to arrive.<br /> <br /> The Beshilu have fallen to the alien radio static that produces MEATWAVE. The Beshilu slowly build a grisly altar of cement blocs and bird skulls, while other congregants prepare for the transmissions to begin.<br /> <br /> The PCs are in town, and as MEATWAVE begins its horrific spread, are caught in the middle.<br /> <br /> Note:<br /> Many thanks to Chris Allen for his awesome MEATWAVE Writeup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T20:18:34-07:00","id":1463371,"title":"","content":"239) It's been five consecutive nights now that the crescent moon has hung in the sky. The luminescent sickle imposes its form upon the black firmament with no sign of change on the horizon. Humans notice in the way humans only ever half-notice anything that isn't grabbing them by the labels and screaming, of course. Maybe the astronomers and meteorologists and Wiccans realize something's up, but they're not exactly rushing to the bullhorns about it for whatever reason. Meanwhile the Ithaeur languish in the spiritual bounty flowing into their werewolf-souls, exploiting the windfall of Essence to fuel strange rites, some of which some of them didn't even realize they knew until the lunar anomaly began, though it's now as though the symbols were always encoded into their blood and bones. The lunes, of course, say nothing helpful, while Pure totems grow agitated and divided on the meaning of it all, debating hotly whether this marks a moment of abruption in the Warden Queen's power or some dread new strengthening of antediluvian bonds among sunlight and gravity and reflection. In the gibbous dark something shifts. A drop of blood falls from nowhere onto a shard of mirror. An act is performed, repeated, then reversed. A lake is like a sea, a road a river. A woman who has been weeping nonstop for five hundred years immediately ceases, stands, and exits her geodic prison. Are the times out of joint, or is this a new good that the law is speaking into existence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T17:38:39-07:00","id":1466068,"title":"","content":"240: Your pack comes across a cold feud between two Pure packs that is starting to heat up.<br /> Neither pack is yet aware of your arrival. What do you do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T17:41:12-07:00","id":1466069,"title":"","content":"241: There was once an old Beshilu who once witnessed the Black Death ravage Europe. It disappeared into the Deep Shadow for a long time. But now it's back, &amp; it's brought the Black Death with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T20:29:38-07:00","id":1466084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/11952-1001-werewolf-story-hooks?p=1466069#post1466069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">241: There was once an old Beshilu who once witnessed the Black Death ravage Europe. It disappeared into the Deep Shadow for a long time. But now it's back, &amp; it's brought the Black Death with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Black Death isn't scary anymore. It actually still infects an average of 650 people every year and kills 1 out of 10 with treatment. Something must be added for this outbreak to cause problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T20:57:37-07:00","id":1466090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/11952-1001-werewolf-story-hooks?p=1466084#post1466084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Black Death isn't scary anymore. It actually still infects an average of 650 people every year and kills 1 out of 10 with treatment. Something must be added for this outbreak to cause problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Black Death&quot; is a distinct event from the general phenomenon of the bubonic plague, and the bubonic plague being kept in check by modern sanitation is distinct from <i>the deadliest pandemic in history</i> being &quot;not scary anymore.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is Werewolf. A 700-year-old rat-demon has come out of the dimension where bits of history take on a life of their own, enhance the things that make them up, and mostly get booted into dormancy rather than actually killed. The Black Death is a spiritually potent event whose return through the channels werewolves are concerned with is going to cause problems by the nature of the metaphysics. Something has already been added to cause problems, and that something is the story hook as described.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T21:49:01-07:00","id":1466092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/11952-1001-werewolf-story-hooks?p=1466090#post1466090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The Black Death&quot; is a distinct event from the general phenomenon of the bubonic plague, and the bubonic plague being kept in check by modern sanitation is distinct from <i>the deadliest pandemic in history</i> being &quot;not scary anymore.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is Werewolf. A 700-year-old rat-demon has come out of the dimension where bits of history take on a life of their own, enhance the things that make them up, and mostly get booted into dormancy rather than actually killed. The Black Death is a spiritually potent event whose return through the channels werewolves are concerned with is going to cause problems by the nature of the metaphysics. Something has already been added to cause problems, and that something is the story hook as described.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200bAdding a layer to the conversation:<br /> <br /> The magics of the Shadow clearly have a lot to do with symbolism, and the particulars of the symbol matters.<br /> <br /> The symbol of the bubonic plague, is, as mentioned, not a whole lot-it's pretty manageable. A rite evoking that is a rite evoking a barrier-not insurmountable, but it slows down certain processes.<br /> <br /> The symbol of the <i>Black Plague</i> is the symbol of one of the worst pandemics in humanity history, with corresponding societal upheaval in just about every term you could care to go over. A rite evoking that is a rite evoking <i>an apocalypse</i>.<br /> <br /> But more importantly, regarding this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/11952-1001-werewolf-story-hooks?p=1466084#post1466084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Black Death isn't scary anymore. It actually still infects an average of 650 people every year and kills 1 out of 10 with treatment. Something must be added for this outbreak to cause problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>why shit on a fun game concept? I can see arguing about how a plot might not actually have enough to it to get into fun with it, but if the plot sounds like fun, then no need to be a kill joy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-01-2021, 01:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T04:15:59-07:00","id":1466111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/11952-1001-werewolf-story-hooks?p=1466084#post1466084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Black Death isn't scary anymore. It actually still infects an average of 650 people every year and kills 1 out of 10 with treatment. Something must be added for this outbreak to cause problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to forget the metaphysics of the spirit world. The black death is the archtype of the plague, the symbol of mass death by disease. Symbols have power in the shadow, and the symbol of the black plague is a lot more dangerous than the real bubonic plague could ever be. Masks and clean environments won't be enough to stop this black death. <br /> <br /> Obviously this rat host has the form of a plague doctor, because people associate that with the black death. And it is considered the heir of the plague king whose death was the start of the rat host. <br /> <br /> The plague prince (as I call him) is obviously a big bad of a chronicle, an idigam level threat. It wouldn't surprise me if dome delusional fire touched started worshiping it while packs of the forsaken and the pure were forced to put aside there differences in the face of such a massive threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T08:57:02-07:00","id":1466131,"title":"","content":"Those are all fair points and I recall what I said. Especially with all the shenanigans a Beshilu can pull for this.<br /> <br /> My only addition is that my intention was less to shit on the idea and more on wanting it a little more elaborated. But it was beyond the scope of the thread, my fault.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-22T01:01:01-08:00","id":1471072,"title":"","content":"242) A relatively sane Magath has come to the pack asking for them to petition the spirit courts for it's inclusion into them.<br /> <br /> Cry on Halloween is a plant/fear spirit, that found harmony despite it's incompatible resonances. But it's concept only makes sense on a single certain day of the year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Dam da namsithim.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12696-lost-his-mind","name":"Lost-His-Mind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12696_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}